window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":4,"qs":[{"id":"E1B-39","d":1,"ts":"1.2.6","t":"Athena CTAS format conversion","q":"A company stores 2 TB of historical CSV files in Amazon S3 that are cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. A data analyst needs to convert the data once into Snappy-compressed Apache Parquet partitioned by year, using only SQL and without provisioning infrastructure. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use the Amazon Redshift COPY command to load the CSV files and then use UNLOAD without specifying a format.","Create an Amazon EMR cluster and run a Hive INSERT OVERWRITE statement.","Configure Amazon Data Firehose to read the CSV files from S3 and convert them to Parquet.","Run an Amazon Athena CREATE TABLE AS SELECT (CTAS) query with format = 'PARQUET', Snappy compression, and partitioned_by = ARRAY['year']."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah konversi satu kali dari CSV ke Parquet terpartisi 'using only SQL' dan 'without provisioning infrastructure'. Athena CTAS adalah query SQL serverless yang membaca tabel sumber dari Data Catalog dan menulis hasilnya ke S3 dalam format Parquet dengan kompresi dan partisi yang ditentukan, sekaligus mendaftarkan tabel baru. Redshift COPY/UNLOAD bisa menghasilkan Parquet jika format ditentukan, tetapi memerlukan cluster Redshift dan UNLOAD tanpa format menghasilkan teks berdelimiter. EMR dengan Hive memerlukan provisioning cluster. Firehose menerima data streaming, bukan membaca file yang sudah ada di S3, dan konversinya hanya untuk input JSON. Aturan umum: konversi format/partisi ad hoc dengan SQL di atas S3 → Athena CTAS (atau INSERT INTO untuk batch tambahan).","r":["Salah — Membutuhkan Redshift, dan UNLOAD tanpa format menghasilkan teks, bukan Parquet.","Salah — EMR memerlukan provisioning dan pengelolaan cluster.","Salah — Firehose memproses aliran data yang masuk, bukan file historis yang sudah ada di S3.","Benar — CTAS Athena mengonversi ke Parquet terpartisi dengan SQL secara serverless."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'convert CSV to Parquet with SQL, serverless, one-time' → Athena CTAS."},{"id":"E1C-66","d":1,"ts":"1.4.8","t":"AWS CDK","q":"A data engineering team writes all of its code in Python. The team wants to define its pipeline infrastructure (Amazon S3 buckets, AWS Glue jobs, Step Functions state machines, and IAM roles) as code by using loops, conditionals, and reusable classes, with IDE autocompletion, while still deploying through AWS CloudFormation. Which tool meets these requirements?","o":["AWS CloudFormation templates written in YAML","AWS CDK in Python","The AWS CLI in a Bash script","AWS Systems Manager Automation documents"],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: infrastruktur ditulis dalam 'Python' dengan 'loops, conditionals, and reusable classes', autocompletion IDE, dan tetap 'deploying through AWS CloudFormation'. AWS CDK memungkinkan Anda mendefinisikan infrastruktur dengan bahasa pemrograman umum (Python, TypeScript, Java, C#, Go); construct tingkat tinggi menyediakan default yang baik, dan CDK melakukan synth ke template CloudFormation sebelum deploy. Distractor terdekat adalah template YAML CloudFormation: tetap IaC, tetapi deklaratif tanpa loop atau class (hanya fungsi intrinsik dan kondisi terbatas). Script AWS CLI bersifat imperatif tanpa manajemen state atau rollback. Dokumen SSM Automation untuk tugas operasional. Aturan umum: IaC dengan bahasa pemrograman → AWS CDK (hasilnya CloudFormation).","r":["Salah — YAML deklaratif tidak mendukung loop atau class seperti bahasa pemrograman.","Benar — CDK Python mendukung konstruksi pemrograman lengkap dan men-deploy melalui CloudFormation.","Salah — Script CLI imperatif tanpa state, rollback, atau CloudFormation.","Salah — SSM Automation untuk runbook operasional, bukan definisi infrastruktur."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'IaC in Python/TypeScript with loops & classes' → AWS CDK (synth ke CloudFormation)."},{"id":"E1A-27","d":1,"ts":"1.1.4","t":"Step Functions for API pagination","q":"A data engineer must backfill 2 years of records from a partner's REST API. The API returns 1,000 records per page with a continuation token, and the full backfill takes about 6 hours of API calls. The engineer wants a serverless solution that can resume from the last successful page if a call fails. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["A single AWS Lambda function that loops through all pages in one invocation.","An Amazon Data Firehose stream with the partner API configured as the source.","An Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes a Lambda function once with a 6-hour timeout.","An AWS Step Functions Standard workflow that loops over a Lambda function, where each invocation processes a batch of pages within the Lambda time limit, passes the continuation token back in the state, and uses Retry for failed calls."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: backfill sekitar '6 hours', pagination dengan 'continuation token', 'serverless', dan 'resume from the last successful page'. Lambda dibatasi maksimum 15 menit per invocation, sehingga satu Lambda tidak bisa menjalankan seluruh backfill. Step Functions (Standard workflow, bisa berjalan hingga 1 tahun) dapat mengulang pemanggilan Lambda yang masing-masing memproses sekumpulan halaman (agar jumlah iterasi tetap jauh di bawah batas 25.000 event history per eksekusi), menyimpan continuation token di state, dan memakai Retry dengan backoff; bila gagal, eksekusi dilanjutkan dari halaman terakhir. Distraktor terdekat adalah satu Lambda dengan loop: melewati batas 15 menit. Timeout 6 jam di Lambda tidak mungkin. Firehose tidak bisa menarik data dari API pihak ketiga. Aturan umum: konsumsi API panjang dengan pagination = Step Functions mengorkestrasi Lambda per halaman.","r":["Salah — Lambda maksimum berjalan 15 menit, jauh di bawah 6 jam.","Salah — Firehose menerima data yang dikirim kepadanya; ia tidak menarik data dari REST API.","Salah — Timeout Lambda maksimum 15 menit; 6 jam tidak dapat dikonfigurasi.","Benar — Step Functions bisa berjalan lama, menyimpan token di state, dan me-retry langkah yang gagal."],"k":"API paginasi > 15 menit → Step Functions loop + Lambda per kumpulan halaman + continuation token di state + Retry."},{"id":"E1C-74","d":1,"ts":"1.4.9","t":"Continuous delivery vs continuous deployment","q":"A data platform team's pipeline automatically builds, tests, and deploys every change to a staging environment. Changes are promoted to production only after a data lead approves them, and every approved change is always in a deployable state. Which term BEST describes this practice?","o":["Continuous integration only","Continuous deployment","Continuous delivery","Blue/green deployment"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya: perubahan otomatis 'builds, tests, and deploys ... to a staging environment', 'always in a deployable state', tetapi produksi hanya setelah 'a data lead approves'. Continuous delivery berarti setiap perubahan otomatis dibangun, diuji, dan disiapkan untuk rilis, dengan langkah rilis ke produksi yang memerlukan keputusan manual. Distractor terdekat adalah continuous deployment: semua perubahan yang lolos tes otomatis langsung ke produksi tanpa persetujuan manusia, sehingga tidak sesuai dengan adanya approval. Continuous integration hanya mencakup penggabungan sering dengan build dan tes otomatis, tanpa deployment ke staging. Blue/green adalah strategi pergantian lingkungan, bukan praktik CI/CD secara keseluruhan. Aturan umum: ada manual approval sebelum produksi → continuous delivery; tanpa approval → continuous deployment.","r":["Salah — CI hanya build dan tes otomatis saat merge, tanpa deployment ke staging.","Salah — Continuous deployment merilis ke produksi otomatis tanpa approval manual.","Benar — Perubahan selalu siap rilis dan produksi memerlukan persetujuan manual.","Salah — Blue/green adalah strategi deployment, bukan praktik keseluruhan ini."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'manual approval before production' → continuous delivery; 'fully automatic to prod' → continuous deployment."},{"id":"E1C-52","d":1,"ts":"1.4.2","t":"Lambda Kinesis parallelization factor","q":"An AWS Lambda function processes records from an Amazon Kinesis data stream with 4 shards. The IteratorAge metric keeps increasing during the day, but the function's average duration is stable and there are no errors. The stream's incoming data rate is within shard limits. The team wants to increase processing throughput without resharding. Which change should the data engineer make?","o":["Configure provisioned concurrency on the function.","Increase the ParallelizationFactor of the event source mapping so that multiple batches from each shard are processed concurrently.","Set reserved concurrency on the function to 4.","Increase the batch window (MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds) to 300 seconds."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejalanya: 'IteratorAge keeps increasing' (konsumen tertinggal) tanpa error, dan syarat 'without resharding'. Secara default Lambda memproses satu batch per shard pada satu waktu; ParallelizationFactor (1–10) memungkinkan hingga 10 batch per shard diproses bersamaan sambil tetap menjaga urutan per partition key. Dengan 4 shard, concurrency bisa naik hingga 40. Distractor terdekat adalah reserved concurrency 4: justru mengunci concurrency pada level yang sekarang (satu per shard), bukan menaikkannya. Provisioned concurrency hanya mengurangi cold start dan tidak mengubah jumlah batch per shard. Batch window lebih panjang menunda pemanggilan dan bisa menambah iterator age. Aturan umum: Kinesis + Lambda tertinggal tanpa reshard → naikkan ParallelizationFactor (atau batch size).","r":["Salah — Tidak mengubah jumlah batch per shard yang diproses bersamaan.","Benar — ParallelizationFactor menambah batch paralel per shard sehingga throughput naik tanpa resharding.","Salah — Membatasi concurrency pada 4 sama saja dengan kondisi sekarang atau lebih buruk.","Salah — Menunggu lebih lama sebelum memanggil fungsi bisa memperbesar keterlambatan."],"k":"Tips ujian: IteratorAge naik + 'no resharding' → ParallelizationFactor (maks 10 per shard)."},{"id":"E3A-51","d":3,"ts":"3.2.2","t":"Cleaning data in Quick Sight datasets","q":"A business analyst builds an Amazon Quick Sight dashboard from an Athena dataset. The source has a revenue column stored as text, some rows with blank region values, and test transactions marked with customer_id 'TEST'. The data engineering team cannot change the upstream pipeline this sprint. The analyst needs correct visuals today. What should the analyst do?","o":["Wait for the next sprint so that the pipeline team can fix the source data.","Use Quick Sight data preparation on the dataset: change the revenue field data type to decimal, add a calculated field that replaces blank regions with 'Unknown', and add a dataset filter that excludes customer_id 'TEST'.","Export the data to a spreadsheet, clean it manually, and upload it as a new dataset every day.","Create visual-level filters on each chart to hide the test rows and ignore the data type issue."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'cannot change the upstream pipeline' dan 'needs correct visuals today'. Quick Sight menyediakan data preparation di level dataset: mengubah tipe data field (teks ke desimal), membuat calculated field untuk mengganti nilai kosong (misalnya dengan fungsi ifelse/isNull), dan filter dataset untuk mengecualikan baris uji. Karena dilakukan di dataset, semua visual dan analisis yang memakai dataset itu otomatis konsisten. Menunggu sprint berikutnya tidak memenuhi kebutuhan hari ini. Pembersihan manual di spreadsheet setiap hari rawan salah dan tidak skalabel. Filter per visual mudah terlewat dan tidak memperbaiki tipe data, sehingga agregasi revenue tetap salah. Aturan umum: perbaikan ringan untuk kebutuhan BI → data prep di dataset Quick Sight; perbaikan permanen tetap sebaiknya di pipeline upstream.","r":["Salah — Tidak memenuhi kebutuhan visual yang benar hari ini.","Benar — Data prep di level dataset memperbaiki tipe data, nilai kosong, dan baris uji untuk semua visual.","Salah — Proses manual harian rawan kesalahan dan tidak skalabel.","Salah — Filter per visual mudah terlewat dan tidak memperbaiki revenue yang bertipe teks."],"k":"Tips ujian: perbaikan cepat untuk dashboard tanpa ubah pipeline → Quick Sight dataset data prep (ubah tipe, calculated field, filter)."},{"id":"E4A-40","d":4,"ts":"4.2.3","t":"Redshift role-based access control","q":"A company uses Amazon Redshift. It defines a set of read privileges for 'reporting' and wants a 'finance_reporting' permission set that includes everything in 'reporting' plus access to the finance schema. The company also wants to assign these permission sets to users and to manage system permissions such as viewing all query activity without making users superusers. Which approach should a data engineer use?","o":["Use Redshift role-based access control: CREATE ROLE reporting and finance_reporting, grant the privileges to the roles, GRANT ROLE reporting TO ROLE finance_reporting, and grant the roles (and system permissions as needed) to users.","Create user groups reporting and finance_reporting and nest the reporting group inside the finance_reporting group.","Make the finance users superusers so that they can see all schemas and all query activity.","Create IAM roles named reporting and finance_reporting with IAM policies that list the allowed Redshift tables."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'includes everything in reporting plus' (hierarki) dan 'system permissions ... without making users superusers'. Redshift role-based access control (RBAC) mendukung pemberian role ke role lain (nesting), sehingga finance_reporting otomatis mewarisi hak reporting. RBAC juga mendukung system permission tertentu (misalnya melihat aktivitas query) yang dapat diberikan ke role, serta system-defined role seperti sys:monitor, tanpa memberi status superuser. User group di Redshift tidak bisa disarangkan (nested) dan tidak bisa memegang system permission. Superuser melanggar least privilege. IAM policy tidak mengatur hak SELECT pada tabel di dalam database Redshift; itu ditangani oleh GRANT di database. Aturan umum: hierarki permission dan system privileges di Redshift → RBAC (CREATE ROLE, GRANT ROLE).","r":["Benar — RBAC Redshift mendukung role bersarang dan system permission tanpa superuser.","Salah — Group Redshift tidak dapat disarangkan dan tidak mendukung system permission.","Salah — Superuser memberi akses penuh dan melanggar least privilege.","Salah — IAM policy tidak mengontrol hak akses tabel di dalam database Redshift."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift role bisa di-grant ke role lain (nested) + system permissions; group tidak bisa nested."},{"id":"E1A-50","d":1,"ts":"1.1.8","t":"AWS Glue VPC connection security groups","q":"A data engineer creates an AWS Glue JDBC connection to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL instance in a private subnet. Test connection fails with a timeout. The RDS security group already allows port 5432 from the Glue connection's security group. Which additional configuration is required for the Glue connection to work?","o":["Add a self-referencing inbound rule to the security group used by the Glue connection that allows all TCP traffic from the same security group.","Make the RDS instance publicly accessible.","Add the AWS Glue service principal to the RDS instance's parameter group.","Attach an Elastic IP address to the RDS instance."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: koneksi JDBC Glue ke RDS di 'private subnet' timeout, padahal RDS sudah mengizinkan port 5432 dari security group Glue. AWS Glue membuat elastic network interface di subnet VPC, dan komponen Glue harus bisa saling berkomunikasi; karena itu security group yang dipakai oleh connection harus memiliki inbound rule self-referencing untuk semua port TCP. Tanpa rule ini, test connection dan job gagal. Distraktor terdekat adalah membuat RDS publik: melemahkan keamanan dan tetap tidak memperbaiki kebutuhan self-referencing. Parameter group mengatur parameter database, bukan izin jaringan, dan Elastic IP tidak berlaku untuk RDS. Aturan umum: Glue connection di VPC = subnet yang tepat + security group self-referencing (all TCP) + akses ke S3 (gateway endpoint atau NAT).","r":["Benar — Glue memerlukan rule inbound self-referencing all TCP pada security group connection agar komponennya dapat berkomunikasi.","Salah — Membuat RDS publik melemahkan keamanan dan tidak menyelesaikan kebutuhan jaringan Glue.","Salah — Parameter group mengatur konfigurasi engine, bukan akses jaringan.","Salah — Elastic IP tidak dapat dilampirkan ke instance RDS dan tidak relevan untuk akses privat."],"k":"Glue JDBC connection timeout di VPC → security group self-referencing inbound all TCP."},{"id":"E3A-39","d":3,"ts":"3.2.1","t":"Quick Sight natural language Q&A","q":"Sales executives want to type questions such as 'What were the top 5 products by revenue in Java last quarter?' and get charts back without asking analysts to build new visuals. The curated sales data is already available as an Amazon Quick Sight dataset. Which solution meets this requirement with the LEAST effort?","o":["Train a custom text-to-SQL model in Amazon SageMaker AI and connect it to Amazon Athena.","Create an Amazon Quick Sight topic on the sales dataset with friendly field names, synonyms, and semantic metadata so that executives can ask natural-language questions (generative BI Q&A).","Build an Amazon Lex chatbot that calls AWS Lambda functions to run predefined SQL queries.","Give executives direct access to the Athena query editor."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'type questions in natural language', 'get charts back', 'dataset already in Quick Sight', dan 'LEAST effort'. Quick Sight menyediakan kemampuan Q&A bahasa alami berbasis generative BI (sebelumnya dikenal sebagai Amazon Q in QuickSight). Anda membuat topic di atas dataset sebagai lapisan semantik, memberi nama field yang ramah, sinonim, dan deskripsi kolom, lalu pengguna bertanya dalam bahasa sehari-hari (kini melalui Amazon Quick chat) dan mendapat jawaban beserta visual. Melatih model text-to-SQL kustom di SageMaker AI adalah pekerjaan ML besar. Lex chatbot dengan query yang sudah ditentukan tidak fleksibel untuk pertanyaan baru. Athena query editor menuntut eksekutif menulis SQL. Aturan umum: 'natural language questions on BI data' → Quick Sight topics/generative BI Q&A. Catatan pembaruan: Amazon QuickSight kini berlanjut sebagai Amazon Quick Sight, fitur di dalam Amazon Quick; pertanyaan bahasa alami atas topic kini diajukan lewat Amazon Quick chat.","r":["Salah — Membangun model ML kustom memerlukan upaya besar dan keahlian ML.","Benar — Topic di Quick Sight menjadi lapisan semantik untuk pertanyaan bahasa alami yang dijawab dengan visual, tanpa membuat chart baru secara manual.","Salah — Chatbot dengan query yang sudah ditentukan tidak bisa menjawab pertanyaan baru secara bebas.","Salah — Eksekutif harus menulis SQL dan tidak mendapatkan chart otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'ask questions in natural language on dashboards' → Quick Sight Q&A topics (generative BI)."},{"id":"E2C-16","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Glue DynamicFrame ResolveChoice","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job reads JSON files from several vendors. The unit_price field is a number in most files but arrives as a quoted string in files from one vendor, so the DynamicFrame shows the field as a choice type and the downstream write to Parquet fails. The data engineer wants all values stored as double without dropping records. What is the MOST appropriate solution?","o":["Apply the ResolveChoice transform with the action cast:double on unit_price before writing.","Apply the ResolveChoice transform with the action make_cols so that both types are kept as separate columns in the final table.","Use the DropNullFields transform to remove the inconsistent records.","Disable schema inference in the crawler and set every column to string in the target table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah tipe data yang berubah antar sumber dan 'stored as double without dropping records'. DynamicFrame di AWS Glue merepresentasikan kolom dengan tipe yang tidak konsisten sebagai choice type, dan transform ResolveChoice menyediakan aksi untuk menyelesaikannya. Aksi cast:double mengonversi semua nilai ke double sehingga schema output konsisten dan tidak ada record yang dibuang. Aksi make_cols menghasilkan dua kolom terpisah (misalnya unit_price_double dan unit_price_string), yang tidak memenuhi syarat satu kolom double. DropNullFields hanya membuang field bernilai null, bukan menyelesaikan konflik tipe, dan tidak relevan untuk menjaga record. Menyetel semua kolom ke string merusak tipe data untuk analitik. Aturan umum: choice type di DynamicFrame → ResolveChoice (cast, make_cols, make_struct, project) sesuai kebutuhan target.","r":["Benar — cast:double menyeragamkan tipe unit_price tanpa membuang record sehingga penulisan Parquet berhasil.","Salah — make_cols memecah field menjadi dua kolom bertipe berbeda, bukan satu kolom double.","Salah — DropNullFields menghapus field null dan tidak menyelesaikan konflik tipe; record yang bermasalah bisa hilang.","Salah — Mengubah semua kolom menjadi string menghilangkan tipe numerik yang dibutuhkan untuk analitik."],"k":"Tips ujian: DynamicFrame choice type (tipe kolom campur) → ResolveChoice cast:<type>."},{"id":"E3B-05","d":3,"ts":"3.3.1","t":"Querying CloudTrail logs with Athena","q":"A compliance team must investigate API activity of a specific IAM role over the last 2 years. The CloudTrail logs are stored as gzip-compressed JSON files in an S3 bucket organized by account, Region, and date, totaling 6 TB. Investigations happen a few times per month. Which solution is the MOST cost-effective?","o":["Load all CloudTrail logs into a provisioned Amazon Redshift cluster and query them with SQL.","Ingest all CloudTrail logs into an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain and search with OpenSearch Dashboards.","Launch a long-running Amazon EMR cluster and query the logs with Spark SQL.","Create an Amazon Athena table over the CloudTrail logs with partition projection on account, Region, and date, and filter by userIdentity in queries."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'a few times per month' dan 'MOST cost-effective' untuk data 6 TB yang sudah ada di S3. Athena bersifat serverless dan bayar per data yang dipindai, sehingga cocok untuk investigasi ad hoc yang jarang. Partition projection pada account/Region/date membuat Athena hanya memindai partisi yang relevan tanpa perlu menjalankan crawler atau MSCK REPAIR. Distraktor terdekat adalah OpenSearch, yang memang bagus untuk pencarian, tetapi menyimpan 6 TB di domain yang menyala terus jauh lebih mahal untuk penggunaan jarang. Redshift provisioned dan EMR long-running juga membayar compute yang idle. Aturan: log audit di S3 + query ad hoc → Athena dengan partisi.","r":["Salah — Cluster Redshift provisioned berjalan terus dan perlu proses load, mahal untuk query beberapa kali sebulan.","Salah — Domain OpenSearch untuk 6 TB membutuhkan storage dan node yang aktif terus, tidak hemat biaya untuk penggunaan jarang.","Salah — EMR long-running membayar cluster idle sepanjang waktu.","Benar — Athena serverless bayar per scan, dan partition projection meminimalkan data yang dipindai tanpa maintenance partisi."],"k":"Tips ujian: query log CloudTrail di S3 secara ad hoc dan murah → Athena + partition projection."},{"id":"E1B-27","d":1,"ts":"1.2.3","t":"Integrating SaaS and database sources","q":"A company needs to combine opportunity data from Salesforce with order data from an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database every day. The combined dataset must be written to Amazon S3 as Parquet for analysis. The company wants a managed solution with the LEAST custom code. Which TWO steps should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Write an AWS Lambda function that pages through the Salesforce REST API and handles OAuth token refresh.","Create an Amazon AppFlow flow that transfers the Salesforce objects to Amazon S3 on a daily schedule.","Use AWS DMS with Salesforce as the source endpoint to replicate the data to Amazon S3.","Use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to capture Salesforce changes and deliver them to RDS.","Create an AWS Glue ETL job that reads the AppFlow output from S3 and the RDS table through a JDBC connection, joins them, and writes Parquet to S3."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Penentunya adalah sumber SaaS (Salesforce) dan database relasional (RDS), jadwal harian, output Parquet, dan 'LEAST custom code'. Amazon AppFlow adalah layanan terkelola untuk menarik data dari aplikasi SaaS seperti Salesforce ke S3 dengan jadwal, tanpa menulis kode API atau menangani OAuth sendiri. Setelah data mendarat di S3, AWS Glue ETL job dapat membaca data tersebut sekaligus tabel RDS via JDBC, melakukan join, dan menulis Parquet. Lambda kustom adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi menuntut kode untuk pagination, rate limit, dan token refresh. DMS tidak mendukung Salesforce sebagai source endpoint, dan Kinesis Data Streams tidak menarik data dari Salesforce. Aturan umum: SaaS → AWS → AppFlow; integrasi multi-sumber dan join → Glue.","r":["Salah — Membutuhkan banyak kode kustom untuk API, pagination, dan OAuth.","Benar — AppFlow menarik data Salesforce ke S3 secara terkelola dan terjadwal.","Salah — DMS ditujukan untuk database, bukan aplikasi SaaS seperti Salesforce.","Salah — Kinesis Data Streams tidak memiliki integrasi untuk menarik data dari Salesforce, dan tujuannya pun bukan S3 Parquet.","Benar — Glue menggabungkan data S3 dan RDS lalu menulis output Parquet."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'SaaS (Salesforce, SAP, Zendesk) → S3/Redshift, no code' → Amazon AppFlow."},{"id":"E2A-27","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Purpose-built databases: OpenSearch","q":"A company collects 2 TB per day of application and VPC flow logs. The security team needs full-text search across log messages, near-real-time interactive dashboards, and alerting on suspicious patterns, while keeping 30 days of searchable data. Which data store should a data engineer use?","o":["Amazon OpenSearch Service","Amazon RDS for MySQL with full-text indexes","Amazon DynamoDB with a GSI on the log message","Amazon Neptune"],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'full-text search', 'near-real-time interactive dashboards', 'alerting', dan volume log besar. Amazon OpenSearch Service menyediakan inverted index untuk pencarian teks penuh, OpenSearch Dashboards untuk visualisasi interaktif, dan fitur alerting, sehingga sangat cocok untuk analitik log dan keamanan; tiering seperti UltraWarm dapat menekan biaya retensi. Distraktor terdekat adalah RDS MySQL dengan full-text index: secara fungsi ada, tetapi tidak dirancang untuk ingest 2 TB/hari dan pencarian log skala besar. DynamoDB tidak mendukung pencarian teks bebas di dalam atribut. Neptune adalah graph database. Aturan umum: log analytics + full-text search + dashboard → Amazon OpenSearch Service.","r":["Benar — OpenSearch Service dirancang untuk pencarian teks penuh, analitik log near-real-time, dashboard, dan alerting.","Salah — Full-text index MySQL tidak efisien untuk ingest dan pencarian log skala TB per hari.","Salah — GSI DynamoDB hanya mendukung pencocokan key, bukan pencarian kata di dalam teks.","Salah — Neptune untuk traversal relasi graph, bukan pencarian teks log."],"k":"Full-text search + log analytics + dashboards → Amazon OpenSearch Service."},{"id":"E4A-05","d":4,"ts":"4.1.2","t":"IAM groups and customer managed policies","q":"A company has 15 data engineers who each have an IAM user. All of them need the same permissions to manage AWS Glue jobs and read from a curated Amazon S3 bucket. New engineers join every month. The security team wants permissions to be managed in one place with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Attach an inline policy with the required permissions to each engineer's IAM user.","Create an IAM role with the required permissions and set its trust policy to allow the IAM group of engineers as the principal.","Create an IAM group, attach a customer managed policy with the required permissions to the group, and add each engineer's IAM user to the group.","Add a bucket policy to the curated bucket that lists the IAM group ARN as the principal, and attach AWS managed Glue policies to each user."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'same permissions', 'new engineers join every month', dan 'managed in one place'. IAM group adalah cara bawaan untuk memberi set permission yang sama ke banyak IAM user; engineer baru cukup ditambahkan ke grup. Menempelkan customer managed policy ke grup juga membuat policy bisa di-versioning dan dipakai ulang. Inline policy per user berarti harus mengubah 15+ tempat setiap ada perubahan. IAM group tidak bisa menjadi principal di trust policy atau resource-based policy, sehingga opsi role dengan trust ke grup dan bucket policy dengan ARN grup sama-sama tidak valid. Aturan umum: grup = kumpulan user untuk menempelkan permission; grup bukan identitas dan tidak bisa di-assume atau dirujuk sebagai principal.","r":["Salah — Inline policy per user menimbulkan overhead besar dan rawan tidak konsisten.","Salah — IAM group tidak bisa dijadikan principal di trust policy role.","Benar — Grup dengan customer managed policy memusatkan pengelolaan permission dan cukup menambah anggota untuk engineer baru.","Salah — ARN IAM group tidak valid sebagai principal di bucket policy, dan policy per user tetap menambah overhead."],"k":"Tips ujian: IAM group tidak bisa jadi principal (trust/bucket policy) dan tidak bisa nested; gunakan grup untuk menempelkan policy ke banyak user."},{"id":"E3B-16","d":3,"ts":"3.3.2","t":"Amazon Managed Grafana authentication and data sources","q":"A company uses Okta as its identity provider and does not use AWS IAM Identity Center. Site reliability engineers need managed dashboards and alert rules that visualize Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus metrics from EKS-based ingestion services alongside CloudWatch metrics from Amazon Data Firehose. The company wants to avoid running any dashboard infrastructure. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Amazon Quick (formerly Amazon QuickSight) dashboard that reads the Prometheus metrics directly.","Create CloudWatch dashboards and grant engineers IAM users with console passwords.","Deploy Grafana on Amazon EC2 and configure Okta OIDC login.","Create an Amazon Managed Grafana workspace with SAML 2.0 authentication federated to Okta, and add the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus and CloudWatch data sources."],"a":[3],"e":"Persyaratannya: identitas dari 'Okta' tanpa IAM Identity Center, menggabungkan metrik Prometheus dan CloudWatch, serta 'avoid running any dashboard infrastructure'. Amazon Managed Grafana mendukung dua metode autentikasi pengguna — SAML 2.0 (misalnya Okta) dan IAM Identity Center, salah satu atau keduanya per workspace —, dan memiliki data source bawaan untuk Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus dan CloudWatch, termasuk Grafana alerting. Distraktor terdekat adalah Grafana di EC2 dengan Okta: secara fungsi bisa, tetapi melanggar syarat tanpa infrastruktur. Amazon Quick (dulu QuickSight) adalah alat BI, bukan alat monitoring metrik Prometheus. IAM user per engineer bukan federasi Okta, dan CloudWatch dashboards bukan alat utama untuk metrik Prometheus. Aturan: Grafana terkelola + IdP pihak ketiga → Managed Grafana dengan SAML.","r":["Salah — Amazon Quick adalah alat BI, bukan alat monitoring operasional untuk metrik Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus dan alert rule.","Salah — IAM user per engineer bertentangan dengan federasi Okta, dan CloudWatch dashboards bukan alat utama untuk memvisualisasikan metrik Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus.","Salah — Menjalankan Grafana di EC2 melanggar syarat tanpa infrastruktur dashboard.","Benar — Managed Grafana mendukung SAML 2.0 dengan Okta dan data source Prometheus serta CloudWatch tanpa server."],"k":"Tips ujian: Managed Grafana auth = IAM Identity Center atau SAML 2.0 (Okta, Azure AD, dll.)."},{"id":"E4A-52","d":4,"ts":"4.2.5","t":"Role-based access control with federation","q":"A company has three job functions on its data platform: data engineers, data analysts, and data scientists. Each function needs a consistent set of permissions across AWS Glue, Amazon Athena, Amazon S3, and Amazon SageMaker AI. Employees sign in through the corporate identity provider, and employees change job functions several times a year. Which authorization approach meets these requirements with the LEAST administrative effort?","o":["Create one IAM role per job function with the required permissions, and map each identity provider group to the matching role through federation.","Create an IAM user for each employee and attach the policies for the employee's job function directly to the user.","Write a single IAM policy that lists every employee's user name in the Principal element.","Create S3 bucket policies that grant access to each employee individually."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'job functions', 'consistent set of permissions', 'sign in through the corporate identity provider', dan sering pindah fungsi. Ini adalah role-based access control (RBAC): permission dikelompokkan per peran pekerjaan dalam IAM role, lalu grup di IdP dipetakan ke role melalui federasi. Ketika karyawan berpindah fungsi, cukup ubah keanggotaan grup di IdP tanpa mengubah policy IAM. IAM user per karyawan menambah credential jangka panjang dan pekerjaan setiap kali fungsi berubah. Principal di identity-based policy tidak digunakan, dan daftar nama individu tidak skalabel. Bucket policy per individu hanya mencakup S3 dan sulit dikelola. Aturan umum: sedikit peran stabil dengan banyak orang → RBAC (role per job function + federasi grup).","r":["Benar — Role per job function yang dipetakan dari grup IdP memberi permission konsisten dan mudah saat karyawan pindah fungsi.","Salah — IAM user per karyawan menambah overhead dan credential jangka panjang.","Salah — Identity-based policy tidak memakai elemen Principal, dan daftar individu tidak skalabel.","Salah — Hanya mencakup S3 dan menuntut pengelolaan per individu."],"k":"Tips ujian: akses per job function + IdP perusahaan → RBAC dengan IAM role per fungsi dan federasi grup."},{"id":"E4A-29","d":4,"ts":"4.2.1","t":"Custom IAM policy instead of managed policy","q":"An AWS Glue job role currently has the AWS managed policy AmazonS3FullAccess attached. A security review requires that the job be able to write objects only to the raw/ prefix of the bucket ingest-prod and nothing else in Amazon S3. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Edit the AmazonS3FullAccess policy to change its Resource element to the raw/ prefix.","Replace AmazonS3FullAccess with a customer managed policy that allows s3:PutObject only on arn:aws:s3:::ingest-prod/raw/*.","Keep AmazonS3FullAccess and add a bucket policy on ingest-prod that allows the role to write to raw/.","Replace AmazonS3FullAccess with the AWS managed policy AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'only to the raw/ prefix ... and nothing else'. AWS managed policy bersifat generik dan dikelola AWS, sehingga tidak bisa diedit dan sering terlalu luas untuk kebutuhan spesifik. Ketika managed policy tidak sesuai, buat customer managed policy dengan action dan resource yang tepat, di sini s3:PutObject pada ARN objek ingest-prod/raw/*. Mempertahankan AmazonS3FullAccess dan menambah bucket policy tidak mengurangi akses, karena allow di IAM tetap berlaku untuk semua bucket lain. AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess tidak memberi izin menulis sama sekali. Aturan umum: managed policy tidak bisa dimodifikasi; jika terlalu luas, ganti dengan custom policy yang dibatasi resource ARN.","r":["Salah — AWS managed policy tidak bisa diedit oleh pelanggan.","Benar — Customer managed policy dengan PutObject pada ARN prefix raw/ memberi tepat akses yang dibutuhkan.","Salah — Bucket policy tambahan tidak mencabut akses penuh S3 dari managed policy yang tetap terpasang.","Salah — Read-only tidak mengizinkan job menulis ke raw/."],"k":"Tips ujian: managed policy terlalu luas → buat customer managed policy dengan Resource ARN spesifik (bucket/prefix/*)."},{"id":"E3A-17","d":3,"ts":"3.1.5","t":"Amazon Redshift Data API","q":"A data engineer is building an AWS Lambda function that runs SQL statements against an Amazon Redshift Serverless workgroup. The function is invoked thousands of times per day, sometimes in bursts. The engineer wants to avoid bundling database drivers and managing persistent database connections, and wants to retrieve results asynchronously. Which approach should the data engineer use?","o":["Package the Redshift JDBC driver in a Lambda layer and open a connection in each invocation.","Put Amazon RDS Proxy in front of the Redshift Serverless workgroup and connect through it.","Use the Amazon Redshift Data API: call ExecuteStatement, check status with DescribeStatement, and read rows with GetStatementResult, using AWS Secrets Manager or temporary IAM credentials.","Query the data through Redshift Spectrum by creating an external schema."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'avoid bundling database drivers', 'no persistent connections', dan 'retrieve results asynchronously'. Amazon Redshift Data API adalah API HTTPS untuk menjalankan SQL di cluster provisioned maupun Redshift Serverless tanpa driver dan tanpa koneksi persisten. Alurnya: ExecuteStatement mengembalikan ID, DescribeStatement untuk status, GetStatementResult untuk hasil, dengan autentikasi lewat Secrets Manager atau kredensial IAM sementara. Ini ideal untuk Lambda yang dipanggil secara burst karena tidak ada connection storm. Driver JDBC di Lambda menambah ukuran paket dan banyak koneksi saat burst. RDS Proxy hanya untuk RDS dan Aurora, tidak untuk Redshift. Spectrum adalah fitur query data S3, bukan cara mengakses Redshift dari aplikasi. Aturan umum: akses Redshift dari Lambda/aplikasi serverless → Redshift Data API.","r":["Salah — Membutuhkan driver dan membuka banyak koneksi saat burst, persis yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — RDS Proxy mendukung RDS dan Aurora, bukan Amazon Redshift.","Benar — Data API tidak butuh driver maupun koneksi persisten, dan asinkron (ExecuteStatement/DescribeStatement/GetStatementResult).","Salah — Spectrum digunakan untuk membaca data di S3 dari Redshift, bukan antarmuka aplikasi ke Redshift."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Lambda + Redshift tanpa driver/koneksi' → Redshift Data API."},{"id":"E3A-56","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Redshift Spectrum hot/cold data","q":"An Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster stores 7 years of sales data, but analysts query data older than 13 months only a few times per quarter. Storage costs are growing, and the company wants to keep all history queryable with standard SQL from Redshift, including joins between recent and historical data. Which TWO steps should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Unload sales data older than 13 months to Amazon S3 as partitioned Parquet files and delete it from the local tables.","Create an external schema in Redshift that references the AWS Glue Data Catalog database containing the historical table, and query it with Redshift Spectrum.","Take a manual snapshot of the cluster and restore it whenever an analyst needs historical data.","Move the historical data to Amazon DynamoDB and query it with PartiQL.","Increase the number of nodes in the cluster to hold the growing history."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'older data queried rarely', 'storage costs are growing', dan 'keep all history queryable with standard SQL from Redshift, including joins'. Pola hot/cold di Redshift: data dingin di-UNLOAD ke S3 sebagai Parquet yang dipartisi (penyimpanan murah), lalu didaftarkan di Glue Data Catalog dan diakses lewat external schema dengan Redshift Spectrum. Query SQL di Redshift tetap bisa menggabungkan tabel lokal (data panas) dan tabel eksternal (data dingin), sering kali dibungkus dalam late-binding view. Restore snapshot setiap kali dibutuhkan lambat dan mahal. DynamoDB tidak cocok untuk query analitik dan join dengan Redshift. Menambah node menaikkan biaya, berlawanan dengan tujuan. Aturan umum: data warehouse yang jarang diakses → offload ke S3 + Redshift Spectrum.","r":["Benar — UNLOAD ke Parquet yang dipartisi di S3 memindahkan data dingin ke penyimpanan murah yang efisien untuk dipindai.","Benar — External schema dan Spectrum membuat data di S3 tetap bisa di-query dan di-join dari Redshift dengan SQL.","Salah — Restore snapshot lambat dan mahal untuk akses rutin per kuartal.","Salah — DynamoDB tidak dirancang untuk analitik SQL atau join dengan Redshift.","Salah — Menambah node menaikkan biaya, berlawanan dengan tujuan penghematan."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift 'cold historical data, keep queryable' → UNLOAD ke S3 (Parquet) + Redshift Spectrum."},{"id":"E3A-28","d":3,"ts":"3.1.7","t":"Athena UNLOAD vs CTAS","q":"A data engineer runs an Amazon Athena query that joins and filters several large tables. The result, about 200 GB, must be written to Amazon S3 as compressed Parquet files so that an Amazon EMR job can read it. The engineer does not want to create a new table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Which Athena feature should the data engineer use?","o":["A CREATE TABLE AS SELECT (CTAS) statement with format = 'PARQUET'.","An UNLOAD statement with format = 'PARQUET' and compression set, writing to the target S3 location.","Download the query result CSV file from the Athena console and convert it with an AWS Lambda function.","An INSERT INTO statement into an existing CSV table."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'written to S3 as compressed Parquet' dan 'not want to create a new table in the Data Catalog'. Pernyataan UNLOAD di Athena menulis hasil query SELECT ke S3 dalam format pilihan (Parquet, ORC, Avro, JSON, atau teks) dengan kompresi, tanpa membuat tabel di katalog. Ini cocok untuk menyerahkan hasil ke sistem lain seperti EMR. CTAS juga menulis Parquet, tetapi selalu membuat tabel baru di Glue Data Catalog, sehingga melanggar syarat. File hasil default Athena berformat CSV, dan mengonversinya dengan Lambda untuk 200 GB tidak praktis. INSERT INTO ke tabel CSV tidak menghasilkan Parquet. Aturan umum: hasil query ke S3 tanpa tabel → UNLOAD; hasil query sebagai tabel baru → CTAS.","r":["Salah — CTAS selalu mendaftarkan tabel baru di Glue Data Catalog.","Benar — UNLOAD menulis hasil query ke S3 dalam Parquet terkompresi tanpa membuat tabel.","Salah — Proses manual, berformat CSV, dan Lambda tidak cocok untuk konversi 200 GB.","Salah — Menulis ke tabel CSV yang sudah ada, bukan Parquet."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'export query result ke S3 dalam Parquet, tanpa tabel' → UNLOAD; 'buat tabel dari query' → CTAS."},{"id":"E4B-40","d":4,"ts":"4.5.1","t":"Redshift data sharing within an account","q":"A company runs an ETL Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster (RA3) that loads sales data every hour. A separate Redshift Serverless workgroup in the same account is used by the BI team. The BI team must query the latest sales tables without copying data, and the ETL cluster's workload must not be affected by BI queries. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["On the producer cluster, create a datashare, add the sales schema and tables to it, and grant usage on the datashare to the consumer namespace; on the consumer, create a database from the datashare.","Run UNLOAD on the ETL cluster every hour and COPY the files into the Redshift Serverless workgroup.","Restore the latest automated snapshot of the ETL cluster into the Redshift Serverless workgroup every hour.","Create Redshift Spectrum external tables in the consumer that point to the producer cluster's managed storage."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'latest sales tables without copying data' dan 'workload must not be affected by BI queries'. Redshift data sharing memberi akses live dan transaksional konsisten dari producer (RA3 atau Serverless) ke consumer namespace tanpa menyalin data; query dijalankan memakai compute milik consumer, sehingga beban BI tidak mengganggu cluster ETL. Langkahnya: CREATE DATASHARE, ALTER DATASHARE ADD SCHEMA/TABLE, GRANT USAGE ON DATASHARE TO NAMESPACE, lalu di consumer CREATE DATABASE FROM DATASHARE. Distraktor terdekat adalah UNLOAD/COPY per jam: menyalin data, menambah pipeline, dan data tertinggal hingga satu jam. Restore snapshot tiap jam berat dan juga salinan basi. Spectrum hanya membaca data di Amazon S3, bukan managed storage cluster lain. Aturan umum: berbagi data Redshift live tanpa salinan dan dengan isolasi compute → Redshift data sharing.","r":["Benar — Datashare memberi akses live tanpa salinan dan query memakai compute consumer.","Salah — UNLOAD/COPY menyalin data dan membuatnya tertinggal hingga satu jam.","Salah — Restore snapshot tiap jam berat, menyalin data, dan tidak memberikan data terbaru.","Salah — Spectrum membaca data di S3, bukan storage terkelola cluster Redshift lain."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'share live Redshift data, no copy, workload isolation' → Redshift data sharing (datashare → namespace)."},{"id":"E3B-44","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"Alerting on Glue Data Quality results","q":"A data engineer runs AWS Glue Data Quality evaluations in several ETL jobs. When a ruleset fails, the data stewards must receive an email immediately. The engineer wants to use built-in integrations and avoid custom polling code. Which TWO solutions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches AWS Glue Data Quality evaluation result events with a failed outcome and targets an Amazon SNS topic.","Publish the data quality results to Amazon CloudWatch from the Evaluate Data Quality transform and create a CloudWatch alarm on the failed-rules metric that notifies an Amazon SNS topic.","Schedule an AWS Lambda function every 10 minutes that calls the Glue API to list data quality results and emails failures.","Enable CloudTrail log file integrity validation.","Run a daily Amazon Athena query on the data quality results stored in Amazon S3 and email the output."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Persyaratannya: 'immediately', 'built-in integrations', dan 'avoid custom polling code'. AWS Glue Data Quality mengirim event 'Data Quality Evaluation Results Available' ke Amazon EventBridge setelah setiap evaluasi ruleset (opsi 'Publish metrics to Amazon CloudWatch', yang aktif secara default, harus tetap dipilih), sehingga rule EventBridge yang memfilter hasil gagal dapat langsung menarget SNS. Selain itu, transform Evaluate Data Quality dapat mempublikasikan metrik glue.data.quality.rules.passed dan glue.data.quality.rules.failed ke CloudWatch, dan alarm pada metrik rules.failed dapat mengirim notifikasi ke SNS. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda polling setiap 10 minutes — berfungsi, tetapi berupa kode polling kustom dan tidak segera. Query Athena harian jauh dari 'immediately'. Integrity validation CloudTrail tidak terkait. Aturan: hasil Glue DQ → EventBridge event atau CloudWatch metric → SNS.","r":["Benar — Glue Data Quality mengirim event hasil evaluasi ke EventBridge yang dapat langsung meneruskan ke SNS.","Benar — Metrik hasil DQ di CloudWatch dapat diberi alarm yang memicu notifikasi SNS.","Salah — Polling dengan Lambda adalah kode kustom dan menimbulkan jeda.","Salah — Integrity validation hanya membuktikan keaslian log CloudTrail.","Salah — Query harian tidak memberi notifikasi segera."],"k":"Tips ujian: notifikasi Glue DQ gagal → EventBridge rule atau CloudWatch alarm → SNS."},{"id":"E3B-27","d":3,"ts":"3.3.8","t":"Log analytics with OpenSearch Service","q":"A company collects application logs from dozens of AWS Glue, Lambda, and containerized ingestion services in CloudWatch Logs. The operations team wants near-real-time full-text search across all logs, complex aggregations, and interactive dashboards, with the logs kept searchable for 1 year in a search index. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use CloudWatch Logs subscription filters to stream the logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service and build visualizations in OpenSearch Dashboards.","Export the logs to Amazon S3 daily and query them with Amazon Athena.","Use CloudWatch Logs Insights saved queries and set the retention to 1 year.","Load the logs into Amazon Redshift every hour with the COPY command."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratannya: 'near-real-time full-text search', 'complex aggregations', 'interactive dashboards', dan 'searchable ... in a search index'. Amazon OpenSearch Service adalah mesin pencarian dan analitik log yang dirancang untuk full-text search dan dashboard interaktif (OpenSearch Dashboards); subscription filter CloudWatch Logs dapat mengalirkan log secara near real time ke domain OpenSearch. Distraktor terdekat adalah Logs Insights: cocok untuk query ad hoc, tetapi bukan search index dengan dashboard eksplorasi kaya seperti OpenSearch Dashboards. Ekspor harian ke S3 + Athena tidak near real time. Redshift adalah data warehouse, bukan mesin full-text search. Aturan: log analytics + full-text search + dashboard → OpenSearch Service.","r":["Benar — Subscription filter mengalirkan log hampir real time ke OpenSearch untuk full-text search dan dashboard interaktif.","Salah — Ekspor harian tidak near real time dan Athena bukan mesin full-text search.","Salah — Logs Insights bagus untuk query ad hoc tetapi bukan search index dengan dashboard eksploratif yang diminta.","Salah — Redshift tidak dirancang untuk full-text search log dan load per jam tidak near real time."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'full-text search + log analytics dashboards' → Amazon OpenSearch Service."},{"id":"E4B-52","d":4,"ts":"4.5.5","t":"Data sovereignty with Region selection","q":"An Indonesian financial services company is subject to a regulation that requires customer transaction data to be stored and processed only within Indonesia. The company is designing a new data lake and analytics platform on AWS. Which approach BEST maintains data sovereignty?","o":["Deploy all storage, ETL, and analytics resources in the Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region, create the AWS KMS keys in that Region, and attach IAM policies that deny actions when aws:RequestedRegion is not ap-southeast-3.","Store the data in the Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region and encrypt it with a customer managed AWS KMS key.","Store the data in the Jakarta Region but run the ETL jobs in the Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region to reduce cost.","Use Amazon CloudFront to cache the data in edge locations close to users in Indonesia."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: data harus 'stored and processed only within Indonesia'. Kedaulatan data (data sovereignty) di AWS terutama dicapai dengan memilih Region yang berada di yurisdiksi tersebut; AWS tidak memindahkan data pelanggan keluar dari Region yang dipilih tanpa tindakan pelanggan. Menempatkan storage, ETL, analitik, dan KMS key di Region Asia Pacific (Jakarta) memenuhi syarat penyimpanan sekaligus pemrosesan, dan IAM policy dengan kondisi aws:RequestedRegion yang menolak Region lain mencegah kesalahan konfigurasi (di AWS Organizations, kontrol yang sama dapat dipusatkan dengan SCP). Distraktor terdekat adalah Singapore + enkripsi KMS: enkripsi tidak mengubah lokasi fisik data, sehingga data tetap tersimpan di luar Indonesia. Menjalankan ETL di Singapore berarti data diproses di luar Indonesia. CloudFront menyalin konten ke edge location dan tidak menjamin lokasi pemrosesan. Aturan umum: data sovereignty → pilih Region yang tepat + kunci di Region yang sama + kontrol preventif pembatasan Region.","r":["Benar — Semua penyimpanan, pemrosesan, dan kunci berada di Region Jakarta, diperkuat IAM policy pembatasan Region (aws:RequestedRegion).","Salah — Enkripsi tidak mengubah fakta bahwa data tersimpan di luar Indonesia.","Salah — Pemrosesan ETL di Singapore melanggar syarat pemrosesan di Indonesia.","Salah — CloudFront menyalin data ke edge location dan tidak menjamin data tetap di yurisdiksi."],"k":"Tips ujian: data sovereignty/residency → Region selection (+ Region-local KMS keys + Region restriction via aws:RequestedRegion); encryption ≠ residency."},{"id":"E2A-04","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Redshift Serverless vs provisioned","q":"A small finance team runs SQL reports on a 2 TB data warehouse only during the first three business days of each month. The query load during those days is unpredictable. The team has no administrators and wants to pay nothing for compute when no queries are running. Which solution is MOST cost-effective?","o":["Deploy an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster with RA3 nodes and keep it running all month.","Deploy an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster and manually pause it after month-end reporting.","Use Amazon Redshift Serverless.","Launch a long-running Amazon EMR cluster with Apache Hive for the reports."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'only during the first three business days', 'unpredictable' load, 'no administrators', dan 'pay nothing for compute when no queries are running'. Amazon Redshift Serverless otomatis menyediakan dan menskalakan kapasitas (RPU) sesuai beban, dan compute hanya ditagih saat query berjalan; storage tetap ditagih terpisah. Distraktor terdekat adalah cluster provisioned yang di-pause manual: biaya compute berhenti saat pause, tetapi tim harus mengelola jadwal pause/resume dan ukuran cluster tetap tidak adaptif terhadap beban yang tidak terduga. Cluster yang menyala sepanjang bulan membayar compute idle. EMR dengan Hive menambah overhead operasional dan tidak sesuai untuk tim tanpa admin. Aturan umum: beban intermiten/tidak terduga, tanpa admin → Redshift Serverless.","r":["Salah — Cluster provisioned yang menyala terus membayar compute selama 27 hari tanpa query.","Salah — Pause manual mengurangi biaya, tetapi menambah pekerjaan operasional dan kapasitas tetap tidak menskalakan otomatis.","Benar — Redshift Serverless menskalakan otomatis dan hanya menagih compute saat ada workload, tanpa perlu admin cluster.","Salah — Cluster EMR long-running membayar instance idle dan membutuhkan keahlian operasional Hadoop."],"k":"Intermittent/unpredictable SQL analytics + no admins → Redshift Serverless (bayar compute saat dipakai)."},{"id":"E1C-17","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"MWAA worker auto scaling","q":"An Amazon MWAA environment runs fine most of the day, but every night between 00:00 and 02:00 hundreds of DAG tasks start at once. During this window tasks sit in the queued state for a long time and the pipeline misses its SLA. CPU utilization on the workers is consistently high during the window, and low the rest of the day. Which solution will resolve the issue MOST cost-effectively?","o":["Increase the maximum worker count of the environment so MWAA automatically scales out workers during the peak and scales back in afterwards.","Set the minimum worker count equal to the maximum worker count so that all workers run all day.","Increase the number of schedulers in the environment.","Move the DAG files to a larger Amazon S3 bucket class with higher throughput."],"a":[0],"e":"Gejalanya: task 'queued' lama dan worker CPU tinggi hanya pada jendela puncak, dengan syarat 'MOST cost-effectively'. MWAA mendukung auto scaling worker antara jumlah minimum dan maksimum; menaikkan maksimum membuat worker bertambah saat antrean task menumpuk dan berkurang kembali setelahnya, jadi Anda hanya membayar kapasitas tambahan saat dibutuhkan. Distractor terdekat adalah menyamakan minimum dengan maksimum: menyelesaikan antrean tetapi membayar worker penuh sepanjang hari meskipun beban rendah. Menambah scheduler membantu jika scheduler yang menjadi bottleneck, bukan ketika worker sudah penuh CPU. S3 tidak punya 'bucket class' yang mempercepat eksekusi task. Aturan umum: task MWAA mengantre karena worker penuh → naikkan max workers (atau environment class), bukan min workers.","r":["Benar — Auto scaling worker menambah kapasitas hanya saat puncak, sehingga SLA terpenuhi dengan biaya minimal.","Salah — Worker penuh sepanjang hari menambah biaya padahal beban rendah di luar jendela puncak.","Salah — Bottleneck ada pada worker (CPU tinggi), bukan pada scheduler.","Salah — Lokasi DAG di S3 tidak memengaruhi kapasitas eksekusi task."],"k":"Tips ujian: MWAA task queued + worker sibuk → tingkatkan maximum workers (auto scaling)."},{"id":"E3B-63","d":3,"ts":"3.4.4","t":"Systematic sampling bias","q":"A factory sensor emits one reading per second. Every 60th reading is an automatic calibration value that is much lower than normal readings. A data engineer took a quality-check sample by keeping every 60th record starting at the first record, and the sample shows that 100% of readings are abnormally low. What is the MOST likely cause, and what should the engineer do?","o":["The sample is too small; keep every 60th record but over a longer time period.","Systematic sampling aligned with the periodic calibration pattern, which biased the sample; use simple random sampling instead.","The sensor is faulty; replace the sensor and resample.","Stratified sampling was used incorrectly; switch to cluster sampling by hour."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'every 60th reading is a calibration value' dan sampel diambil 'every 60th record'. Systematic sampling (setiap item ke-k) berisiko bias besar jika interval sampling selaras dengan pola periodik dalam data; di sini interval 60 tepat mengenai nilai kalibrasi sehingga 100% sampel terlihat abnormal. Simple random sampling memutus keselarasan dengan pola periodik dan menghasilkan sampel yang representatif. Distraktor terdekat adalah memperpanjang periode dengan interval yang sama — tetap mengenai titik kalibrasi yang sama, jadi bias tidak hilang. Menyimpulkan sensor rusak adalah kesimpulan keliru akibat sampling. Cluster sampling per jam tetap memasukkan pola kalibrasi dan bukan perbaikan yang tepat untuk kasus ini. Aturan: data periodik + systematic sampling = risiko bias → gunakan random sampling.","r":["Salah — Interval yang sama tetap selaras dengan pola kalibrasi sehingga bias tetap ada.","Benar — Interval sampling yang selaras dengan pola periodik menghasilkan bias; random sampling menghindarinya.","Salah — Masalahnya ada pada teknik sampling, bukan pada sensor.","Salah — Teknik yang digunakan adalah systematic sampling, dan cluster per jam bukan solusi atas keselarasan periodik."],"k":"Tips ujian: systematic sampling + data periodik → bias; gunakan random sampling."},{"id":"E3B-41","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"Validating records in Amazon Data Firehose","q":"An Amazon Data Firehose stream delivers JSON events to Amazon S3. Some events arrive without the required customer_id field. The company wants invalid events kept out of the main S3 prefix but still saved for later remediation, while valid events continue to be delivered. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Enable Firehose data transformation with an AWS Lambda function that returns a result of ProcessingFailed for events without customer_id, so that Firehose writes them to the error output prefix.","Enable record format conversion to Apache Parquet so that invalid events are rejected.","Enable server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys on the destination S3 bucket.","Enable S3 Object Lock on the destination bucket."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya: event tanpa 'customer_id' harus 'kept out of the main S3 prefix but still saved', sementara event valid tetap mengalir. Data transformation Lambda pada Firehose mengembalikan status per record: Ok, Dropped, atau ProcessingFailed. Record dengan ProcessingFailed ditulis Firehose ke error output prefix di S3 (folder processing-failed), sehingga terpisah dari data utama namun tidak hilang. Distraktor terdekat adalah record format conversion ke Parquet: hanya mengubah format dan bisa menggagalkan record karena masalah skema, bukan aturan bisnis, dan tidak dirancang sebagai validasi kehadiran field. Enkripsi KMS hanya melindungi data at rest. Aturan: validasi per record di Firehose → transformation Lambda (Ok/Dropped/ProcessingFailed).","r":["Benar — Status ProcessingFailed membuat Firehose menyimpan record invalid di error prefix sementara record valid tetap terkirim.","Salah — Konversi format tidak menegakkan aturan kehadiran field bisnis.","Salah — Enkripsi melindungi data at rest, tidak memvalidasi atau memisahkan event yang tidak memiliki customer_id.","Salah — Object Lock hanya mencegah penghapusan atau perubahan objek."],"k":"Tips ujian: validasi record streaming di Firehose → transformation Lambda; ProcessingFailed → error prefix."},{"id":"E4B-17","d":4,"ts":"4.3.3","t":"Sharing encrypted Redshift snapshots","q":"A company's Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster is encrypted with a customer managed AWS KMS key in Account A. A partner analytics team in Account B needs to restore a copy of the cluster from a manual snapshot for a one-time investigation. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Encrypted snapshots cannot be shared, so unload all tables to Amazon S3 and share the bucket with Account B.","Enable cross-Region snapshot copy with a snapshot copy grant for Account B.","Authorize Account B to restore the manual snapshot, and update the key policy of the customer managed key in Account A to allow Account B to use the key.","Create a datashare for all schemas and grant usage to Account B."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya adalah 'restore a copy of the cluster from a manual snapshot' di akun lain, sementara snapshot dienkripsi dengan 'customer managed AWS KMS key'. Amazon Redshift mendukung berbagi manual snapshot dengan akun lain melalui authorize snapshot access; untuk snapshot terenkripsi, akun penerima juga harus diberi akses ke KMS key melalui key policy, jika tidak restore akan gagal dengan access denied. Distraktor terdekat adalah cross-Region snapshot copy grant: fitur ini untuk menyalin snapshot ke Region lain dalam akun yang sama, bukan berbagi ke akun lain. UNLOAD ke S3 tidak perlu karena snapshot terenkripsi memang bisa dibagikan, dan prosesnya jauh lebih berat. Datashare memberi akses live ke data, bukan salinan cluster yang dapat di-restore. Aturan umum: share encrypted snapshot lintas akun → authorize snapshot access + bagikan customer managed key melalui key policy.","r":["Salah — Snapshot terenkripsi customer managed key dapat dibagikan; unload/share bucket menambah upaya.","Salah — Snapshot copy grant dipakai untuk copy lintas Region, bukan berbagi lintas akun.","Benar — Authorize snapshot access ke Account B dan izinkan Account B memakai KMS key di key policy.","Salah — Datashare memberi akses data live, bukan cluster salinan yang bisa di-restore untuk investigasi terpisah."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'share encrypted snapshot with another account' → share snapshot + share KMS key (customer managed, bukan AWS managed key)."},{"id":"E2C-27","d":2,"ts":"2.4.4","t":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking","q":"A regulated bank must prove to auditors exactly which training dataset version, processing job, and training job produced each model version that is deployed to an Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint. Models are built with Amazon SageMaker Pipelines. The data engineer wants to capture this information with the LEAST custom development. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking, which automatically records lineage entities for SageMaker Pipelines steps, and query the lineage graph for each model.","Write a custom AWS Lambda function that logs every pipeline step to an Amazon DynamoDB table.","Enable AWS CloudTrail and reconstruct lineage from CreateTrainingJob API calls.","Tag every Amazon S3 object with the model version that used it."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah membuktikan 'which training dataset version, processing job, and training job produced each model version' dengan 'LEAST custom development'. Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking menyimpan entitas lineage (artifact, action, context, association) dan secara otomatis membuat entitas tersebut untuk job dan langkah SageMaker Pipelines, sehingga hubungan data → processing → training → model → endpoint dapat ditelusuri dan di-query. Lambda + DynamoDB kustom berhasil tetapi membutuhkan pengembangan dan pemeliharaan sendiri. CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, tetapi merekonstruksi lineage dari log itu manual dan rapuh. Tag pada objek S3 tidak menggambarkan hubungan antar job dan sulit dipelihara. Aturan umum: lineage workflow ML (dataset → model → endpoint) → SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking.","r":["Benar — ML Lineage Tracking otomatis mencatat entitas lineage untuk SageMaker Pipelines dan dapat di-query per model.","Salah — Solusi kustom menambah pengembangan dan pemeliharaan.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat API call, bukan graph lineage yang siap di-query.","Salah — Tag S3 tidak merepresentasikan hubungan antar job dan model."],"k":"Tips ujian: audit model ML ← dataset/job mana → SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking."},{"id":"E4B-48","d":4,"ts":"4.5.3","t":"Compliant S3 replication","q":"A company in Germany stores customer data in an S3 bucket in eu-central-1. For disaster recovery, the data must have a replica in a second AWS Region. Regulations require that customer data never leave the EU, and the company must prevent anyone except the platform team from changing replication settings later. Which TWO actions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication from the eu-central-1 bucket to a bucket in eu-west-1.","Create an S3 Multi-Region Access Point with buckets in eu-central-1 and us-east-1.","Configure an AWS Backup plan with a copy rule to a backup vault in us-east-1.","Add a statement to the source bucket policy that denies s3:PutReplicationConfiguration and s3:PutBucketPolicy to all principals except the platform team's IAM role.","Enable S3 Object Lock in compliance mode on the source bucket."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Kata kunci: replika di 'a second AWS Region' untuk DR, data 'never leave the EU', dan 'prevent anyone except the platform team from changing replication settings'. Cross-Region Replication ke eu-west-1 memenuhi DR sekaligus tetap di dalam EU. Statement Deny pada bucket policy sumber untuk s3:PutReplicationConfiguration (dan s3:PutBucketPolicy, agar deny itu tidak bisa dihapus) bagi semua principal kecuali role tim platform mencegah pihak lain mengubah tujuan replikasi ke Region non-EU; explicit deny di resource policy berlaku walaupun IAM policy principal tersebut mengizinkan. Distraktor terdekat adalah Multi-Region Access Point: menyediakan routing multi-Region, tetapi menyertakan us-east-1 sehingga data keluar dari EU. Copy rule AWS Backup ke us-east-1 juga melanggar residensi. Object Lock mencegah penghapusan/penimpaan objek, bukan perubahan konfigurasi replikasi atau lokasi data. Aturan umum: DR yang patuh residensi → replikasi hanya ke Region yang diizinkan + kontrol preventif (explicit deny) pada konfigurasi replikasi.","r":["Benar — CRR ke eu-west-1 memenuhi DR dan data tetap di dalam EU.","Salah — Menyertakan bucket di us-east-1 membuat data meninggalkan EU.","Salah — Copy rule ke us-east-1 menyalin backup ke luar EU.","Benar — Explicit deny di bucket policy mencegah selain tim platform mengubah konfigurasi replikasi maupun menghapus deny tersebut.","Salah — Object Lock mengatur imutabilitas objek, bukan konfigurasi replikasi atau lokasi data."],"k":"Tips ujian: DR + data residency → replicate only to allowed Region + explicit deny on s3:PutReplicationConfiguration for everyone except the platform role."},{"id":"E4A-48","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation cross-account sharing","q":"A producer AWS account governs a data lake with AWS Lake Formation. A consumer account in the same organization needs analysts to query two producer tables with Amazon Athena in the consumer account, with access controlled by Lake Formation and without copying the data. Which TWO steps are required? (Choose TWO.)","o":["In the producer account, use Lake Formation to grant SELECT on the two tables (or on a matching LF-Tag expression) to the consumer account, with the grantable option.","In the producer account, add a bucket policy that grants the consumer account s3:GetObject on the whole data lake bucket.","In the consumer account, use AWS DataSync to copy the producer tables into a local S3 bucket every hour.","In the consumer account, have the data lake administrator create resource links to the shared tables and grant the analysts' IAM role permissions on the shared tables and DESCRIBE on the resource links.","In the consumer account, create an IAM policy that allows glue:GetTable on all resources in the producer account's Data Catalog."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'controlled by Lake Formation' dan 'without copying the data'. Lake Formation cross-account sharing bekerja dalam dua tahap: pemilik data di akun producer memberi izin pada tabel (named resource atau LF-Tag) kepada akun consumer, dan Lake Formation memakai AWS RAM di belakang layar untuk membagikannya. Kemudian data lake administrator di akun consumer membuat resource link agar tabel muncul di Data Catalog lokal dan bisa direferensikan Athena, lalu memberi izin kepada principal lokal (izin pada tabel target dan DESCRIBE pada resource link). Grant dengan opsi grantable diperlukan agar admin consumer dapat meneruskan izin ke user lokal. Bucket policy ke seluruh bucket melewati Lake Formation dan terlalu luas. Menyalin dengan DataSync melanggar syarat tanpa salinan. glue:GetTable lintas akun saja tidak memberi akses data yang dikelola Lake Formation. Aturan umum: share Lake Formation lintas akun = grant ke account ID + resource link dan grant lokal di consumer.","r":["Benar — Grant lintas akun dari producer (dengan grantable) adalah langkah pertama berbagi data yang diatur Lake Formation.","Salah — Bucket policy ke seluruh bucket melewati kontrol Lake Formation dan terlalu luas.","Salah — Menyalin data melanggar syarat dan menambah biaya.","Benar — Resource link dan grant lokal memungkinkan analis consumer menemukan dan meng-query tabel lewat Athena.","Salah — Izin Data Catalog saja tidak memberi akses data yang diatur Lake Formation dan wildcard terlalu luas."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lake Formation cross-account → producer grant ke account ID (via RAM) + consumer membuat resource link dan grant ke principal lokal."},{"id":"E1B-04","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Redshift ELT with SQL","q":"A company loads raw sales data into staging tables in an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster every night. Analysts who are proficient only in SQL must transform the staging tables into a star schema in the same cluster. The company wants to avoid moving the data out of Redshift. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Unload the staging tables to Amazon S3, transform the files with an AWS Glue PySpark job, and use the COPY command to load the results back.","Export the staging data to an Amazon EMR cluster with Apache Hive, transform it with HiveQL, and reload it into Redshift.","Write SQL stored procedures in Redshift that transform the staging tables into fact and dimension tables, and run them with the Redshift query scheduler.","Use AWS Lambda functions that read each row through the Redshift JDBC driver, transform it, and insert it into the target tables."],"a":[2],"e":"Frasa penentu adalah 'proficient only in SQL', 'in the same cluster', dan 'avoid moving the data out of Redshift'. Pola ELT di dalam Redshift dengan stored procedure SQL memanfaatkan engine MPP Redshift yang sudah ada, dan bisa dijadwalkan dengan query scheduler (Query Editor v2 / EventBridge) tanpa infrastruktur tambahan. Opsi UNLOAD → Glue → COPY memang bisa, tetapi memindahkan data keluar-masuk Redshift dan menuntut skill PySpark yang tidak dimiliki analis. EMR dengan Hive menambah cluster yang harus dikelola dan juga memindahkan data. Lambda yang memproses baris per baris lewat JDBC sangat lambat dan tidak skalabel. Aturan umum: data sudah ada di Redshift dan tim berbasis SQL → transformasi ELT dengan SQL/stored procedure di Redshift.","r":["Salah — Memindahkan data keluar dan masuk Redshift serta membutuhkan PySpark; melanggar syarat tidak memindahkan data dan skill tim.","Salah — EMR + Hive menambah cluster yang dikelola dan memindahkan data ke luar Redshift.","Benar — Stored procedure SQL memakai kemampuan MPP Redshift, sesuai skill analis, dan dijadwalkan tanpa infrastruktur baru.","Salah — Transformasi baris per baris lewat Lambda dan JDBC lambat, rawan timeout, dan tidak memanfaatkan pemrosesan paralel Redshift."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'data already in Redshift + SQL skills' → ELT dengan stored procedure/SQL di Redshift, bukan export ke Spark."},{"id":"E4B-05","d":4,"ts":"4.3.1","t":"Anonymization and quasi-identifiers","q":"A hospital wants to share a patient visit dataset stored in Amazon S3 with an external university for research. Privacy policy requires that individuals cannot be re-identified. The dataset contains name, national ID, full birth date, 5-digit postal code, gender, diagnosis code, and visit date. The researchers need diagnosis trends by age group and region. Which approach BEST meets the anonymization requirement?","o":["Encrypt the dataset with a customer managed AWS KMS key and grant the university's AWS account permission to use the key.","Hash the name and national ID columns with SHA-256 and share all other columns unchanged.","Use AWS Lake Formation to exclude only the name column from the university's grant.","Remove the direct identifiers, and generalize the quasi-identifiers by converting birth dates to age ranges and truncating postal codes to a larger region before sharing a new copy of the dataset."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'individuals cannot be re-identified' sementara peneliti tetap butuh 'age group and region'. Anonimisasi yang benar harus menangani direct identifier (nama, national ID) dan juga quasi-identifier (tanggal lahir lengkap, kode pos 5 digit, gender) yang jika dikombinasikan dapat mengidentifikasi individu. Menghapus identifier langsung lalu melakukan generalisasi (tanggal lahir → rentang usia, kode pos → wilayah lebih besar) adalah teknik seperti k-anonymity yang tetap mempertahankan nilai analitis. Distraktor terdekat adalah hashing nama dan ID: kolom ini memang tersamarkan, tetapi kombinasi birth date + postal code + gender yang tetap utuh masih memungkinkan re-identifikasi. Enkripsi KMS bukan anonimisasi karena penerima yang punya akses kunci melihat data asli. Mengecualikan kolom nama saja juga masih menyisakan national ID dan quasi-identifier. Aturan umum: anonimisasi = hapus direct identifier + generalisasi/suppress quasi-identifier.","r":["Salah — Enkripsi bukan anonimisasi; universitas yang dapat mendekripsi melihat seluruh data asli.","Salah — Quasi-identifier yang dibiarkan utuh masih memungkinkan re-identifikasi individu.","Salah — National ID dan quasi-identifier tetap terekspos, sehingga individu masih dapat dikenali.","Benar — Menghapus identifier langsung dan menggeneralisasi quasi-identifier mencegah re-identifikasi sambil mempertahankan analisis per usia dan wilayah."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'cannot be re-identified' → tangani quasi-identifier (generalisasi), bukan hanya hash nama/ID; enkripsi ≠ anonimisasi."},{"id":"E1B-15","d":1,"ts":"1.2.1","t":"ECS on Fargate for event-driven processing","q":"A data engineer has packaged a Python transformation into a container image stored in Amazon ECR. The container must run every time a new file is uploaded to a specific S3 prefix, and each run takes about 30 minutes. The team does not want to manage any servers or cluster instances. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Deploy the container image as an AWS Lambda function triggered by S3 event notifications.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for S3 Object Created events that starts an Amazon ECS task on AWS Fargate with the container image.","Create an Amazon ECS cluster with the EC2 launch type and run the container as a long-running service that polls the S3 prefix.","Create an Amazon EKS cluster with a managed node group and run the container as a Kubernetes CronJob every 5 minutes."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhan penentunya adalah dijalankan per file baru (event-driven), durasi 'about 30 minutes', dan 'does not want to manage any servers or cluster instances'. EventBridge dapat menerima event S3 Object Created dan menjalankan ECS RunTask pada Fargate secara langsung, sehingga container berjalan tanpa batas waktu 15 menit dan tanpa instance EC2 yang dikelola. Lambda dengan container image adalah distraktor terdekat karena event-driven dan serverless, tetapi batas 15 menit membuat proses 30 menit gagal. ECS dengan EC2 launch type dan EKS dengan managed node group sama-sama mengharuskan pengelolaan instance, ditambah logika polling atau jadwal yang tidak benar-benar event-driven. Aturan umum: container event-driven yang lebih dari 15 menit tanpa server → EventBridge + ECS on Fargate.","r":["Salah — Lambda container image tetap terkena batas timeout 15 menit.","Benar — EventBridge memicu task Fargate per event; tidak ada server yang dikelola dan tidak ada batas 15 menit.","Salah — EC2 launch type berarti mengelola instance, dan service yang polling membayar compute terus-menerus.","Salah — Node group EKS harus dikelola, dan CronJob berbasis jadwal bukan pemicu per file."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'container + > 15 minutes + no servers + event-driven' → EventBridge → ECS RunTask on Fargate."},{"id":"E1A-38","d":1,"ts":"1.1.6","t":"Glue workflow EventBridge batching","q":"Files arrive in an Amazon S3 bucket at irregular intervals, sometimes hundreds per hour and sometimes a few per day. An AWS Glue workflow processes the files, and starting the workflow for every single file is too expensive. The data engineer wants to start the workflow when 100 files have arrived, or when 15 minutes have passed since the first new file, whichever comes first. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the S3 object-created events that targets the Glue workflow, and configure the workflow's EVENT trigger with a batching condition of 100 events and a 900-second batch window.","Create an S3 Event Notification that invokes a Lambda function to start the workflow for each file.","Schedule the Glue workflow to run every 15 minutes regardless of new files.","Run an AWS Glue crawler every minute and start the workflow when the crawler detects new partitions."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: data datang 'at irregular intervals', mulai saat '100 files' atau '15 minutes', 'whichever comes first'. Glue workflow dapat dimulai oleh event EventBridge melalui trigger bertipe EVENT, dan trigger itu mendukung event batching condition: BatchSize (jumlah event) dan BatchWindow (detik, maksimum 900 detik = 15 menit). Workflow dimulai saat salah satu kondisi terpenuhi lebih dulu. Distraktor terdekat adalah jadwal tiap 15 menit: workflow tetap berjalan walau tidak ada file (biaya sia-sia) dan tidak bereaksi saat 100 file sudah terkumpul. Lambda per file melanggar syarat biaya. Crawler tiap menit mahal dan bukan mekanisme pemicu. Aturan umum: memicu Glue workflow berdasarkan kumpulan event = EventBridge + EVENT trigger dengan batch size/window.","r":["Benar — EVENT trigger dengan batching condition memulai workflow saat 100 event atau 900 detik tercapai lebih dulu.","Salah — Memulai workflow untuk setiap file terlalu mahal sesuai skenario.","Salah — Jadwal tetap berjalan meskipun tidak ada file dan tidak bereaksi saat batch 100 file sudah lengkap.","Salah — Crawler setiap menit mahal dan tidak dirancang sebagai trigger batch."],"k":"Glue workflow dipicu per kumpulan event → EventBridge + EVENT trigger (BatchSize, BatchWindow ≤ 900 s)."},{"id":"E1B-61","d":1,"ts":"1.2.9","t":"Structured vs semi-structured vs unstructured data","q":"A data engineer is cataloging new data sources for a data lake: rows from an Amazon RDS for MySQL orders table, JSON web server logs with optional nested fields, MP4 product videos, and scanned PDF contracts. Which dataset is semi-structured and is BEST suited to schema-on-read with an AWS Glue crawler and Amazon Athena?","o":["The rows from the RDS for MySQL orders table","The JSON web server logs with optional nested fields","The MP4 product videos","The scanned PDF contracts"],"a":[1],"e":"Penentunya adalah istilah 'semi-structured' dan 'schema-on-read'. Data semi-terstruktur seperti JSON, XML, atau Avro memiliki struktur dan tag yang dapat dideskripsikan sendiri, tetapi skemanya fleksibel, misalnya ada field opsional atau bersarang. Glue crawler dapat menginferensi skema dari JSON tersebut, lalu Athena dapat meng-query-nya langsung dari S3. Tabel RDS adalah data terstruktur dengan skema tetap (schema-on-write). Video MP4 dan PDF hasil scan adalah data tidak terstruktur yang membutuhkan ekstraksi (misalnya dengan layanan AI) sebelum bisa di-query dengan SQL. Aturan umum: terstruktur = baris/kolom tetap; semi-terstruktur = JSON/XML/Avro; tidak terstruktur = gambar, video, audio, dokumen bebas.","r":["Salah — Tabel relasional adalah data terstruktur dengan skema tetap.","Benar — Log JSON dengan field opsional dan bersarang adalah data semi-terstruktur yang cocok untuk crawler + Athena.","Salah — Video adalah data tidak terstruktur dan tidak dapat di-query langsung dengan SQL.","Salah — PDF hasil scan adalah data tidak terstruktur yang memerlukan ekstraksi terlebih dahulu."],"k":"Tips ujian: JSON/XML/Avro = semi-structured; tables = structured; images/video/audio/PDF = unstructured."},{"id":"E1C-39","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"Glue job timeout alerts","q":"An AWS Glue job normally finishes in 40 minutes. Occasionally it hangs because of a lock on the source database and runs for many hours, delaying all downstream reports. The team wants the job to stop automatically after 2 hours and to receive an alert when this happens, with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a CloudWatch alarm on the job's CPU utilization that sends an email when CPU is low for 2 hours.","Schedule an AWS Lambda function every 15 minutes that checks the job's elapsed runtime, stops it after 2 hours, and publishes to Amazon SNS.","Set the Glue job timeout to 120 minutes, and create an Amazon EventBridge rule for 'Glue Job State Change' events with state TIMEOUT that targets an Amazon SNS topic.","Ask the on-call engineer to check the Glue console every morning and stop long-running jobs manually."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhan: 'stop automatically after 2 hours' dan 'receive an alert' dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Properti timeout pada Glue job menghentikan run yang melewati batas menit tertentu dan menandai statusnya TIMEOUT; Glue lalu mengirim event 'Glue Job State Change' dengan state TIMEOUT ke EventBridge, yang dapat diteruskan ke SNS untuk notifikasi. Distractor terdekat adalah Lambda terjadwal: bisa bekerja, tetapi Anda menulis logika polling dan stop sendiri untuk fitur yang sudah ada di Glue. Alarm CPU rendah tidak menghentikan job dan bisa menjadi indikator yang salah. Pemeriksaan manual jelas tidak otomatis. Aturan umum: cegah job menggantung → set job timeout; alert → EventBridge state change → SNS.","r":["Salah — Alarm CPU tidak menghentikan job dan bukan indikator yang andal untuk job menggantung.","Salah — Polling kustom menduplikasi fitur timeout bawaan Glue dan menambah kode.","Benar — Timeout bawaan menghentikan job, dan event TIMEOUT diteruskan ke SNS tanpa kode.","Salah — Proses manual tidak memenuhi syarat otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue job 'hang' → job Timeout + EventBridge (state TIMEOUT) → SNS."},{"id":"E1B-28","d":1,"ts":"1.2.3","t":"Redshift Spectrum","q":"A company keeps the most recent 3 months of sales data in Amazon Redshift tables and has moved 7 years of historical sales data to Amazon S3 as partitioned Parquet files cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Analysts need to run occasional Redshift SQL queries that combine recent and historical data. The company does not want to reload the historical data into Redshift. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use the COPY command to load the historical data into temporary tables before each query.","Create an AWS Glue job that merges the historical and recent data into a new set of Redshift tables every night.","Query the historical data with Amazon Athena and the recent data with Redshift, and combine the results in a spreadsheet.","Create an external schema in Redshift that references the Glue Data Catalog database, and use Redshift Spectrum to join the external tables with local tables."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah data historis yang sudah ada di S3 sebagai Parquet terkatalog, query 'occasional' yang menggabungkan data baru dan lama, serta tidak ingin 'reload the historical data into Redshift'. Redshift Spectrum memakai external schema dari Glue Data Catalog sehingga tabel S3 dapat di-join langsung dengan tabel lokal Redshift dalam satu query SQL, dan Parquet terpartisi membuat pemindaian efisien. COPY ke tabel sementara dan Glue job yang menggabungkan ke Redshift sama-sama memuat ulang data historis, melanggar syarat. Menggabungkan hasil Athena dan Redshift secara manual tidak praktis dan rawan kesalahan. Aturan umum: data panas di Redshift + data dingin di S3 dalam satu query → Redshift Spectrum.","r":["Salah — COPY memuat ulang data historis ke Redshift, yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — Glue job memindahkan data historis kembali ke Redshift setiap malam.","Salah — Penggabungan manual di spreadsheet tidak skalabel dan bukan solusi SQL terpadu.","Benar — Spectrum melakukan join tabel eksternal S3 dengan tabel lokal tanpa memuat data."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'join Redshift tables with data in S3 without loading' → Redshift Spectrum (external schema)."},{"id":"E1A-15","d":1,"ts":"1.1.2","t":"AWS Glue partition pushdown","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job reads a 50 TB Amazon S3 dataset that is cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog and partitioned by year, month, and day. The job only needs the data for the previous day, but it currently lists and reads every partition, which makes it slow. What should the data engineer do to read only the required data?","o":["Increase the number of DPUs allocated to the job.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before each job run to update the partitions.","Convert the job to an AWS Glue Python shell job.","Use a push_down_predicate on the year, month, and day partition columns when creating the DynamicFrame from the catalog table."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: dataset 'partitioned by year, month, and day', tetapi job 'only needs the data for the previous day' dan saat ini 'reads every partition'. Dengan push_down_predicate pada kolom partisi, Glue memfilter partisi di level metadata Data Catalog sebelum membaca, sehingga hanya file partisi kemarin yang di-list dan dibaca dari S3. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah DPU: job menjadi lebih cepat, tetapi tetap membaca 50 TB dan biayanya naik. Python shell job tidak terdistribusi sehingga lebih buruk untuk data besar. Menjalankan crawler hanya memperbarui metadata partisi, tidak membatasi data yang dibaca. Aturan umum: filter data terpartisi di Glue = pushdown predicate (partition pruning), bukan menambah kapasitas.","r":["Salah — Menambah DPU menaikkan biaya tetapi job tetap membaca seluruh partisi.","Salah — Crawler memperbarui metadata, tetapi tidak membatasi partisi yang dibaca job.","Salah — Python shell tidak terdistribusi dan tidak cocok untuk dataset besar.","Benar — Pushdown predicate memangkas partisi di level katalog sehingga hanya data kemarin yang dibaca."],"k":"Glue baca data terpartisi lebih sedikit → push_down_predicate (partition pruning)."},{"id":"E2B-21","d":2,"ts":"2.2.5","t":"Glue JDBC connection networking","q":"An AWS Glue crawler and an AWS Glue ETL job must connect to an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster in private subnets of a VPC that has no NAT gateway. The connection test fails. Which TWO configuration changes are required for AWS Glue to connect to the database? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Make the Aurora DB cluster publicly accessible and allow 0.0.0.0/0 on port 5432.","Add a self-referencing inbound rule for all TCP traffic to the security group used by the Glue connection.","Create an S3 gateway VPC endpoint and associate it with the route table of the subnet used by the Glue connection.","Attach an internet gateway directly to the private subnet so that Glue can download drivers.","Create a second Glue connection of type NETWORK in a different VPC and peer the VPCs."],"a":[1,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'private subnets' dan 'no NAT gateway'. Saat memakai Glue connection di VPC, Glue membuat elastic network interface di subnet yang dipilih dengan security group dari connection. Komponen Glue saling berkomunikasi, sehingga security group wajib punya inbound rule self-referencing untuk semua port TCP. Glue juga harus mengakses Amazon S3 (script, driver, temporary directory) dari subnet itu; tanpa NAT, solusinya adalah S3 gateway VPC endpoint di route table subnet tersebut. Membuat database publik melanggar praktik keamanan dan tidak memperbaiki akses ke S3. Internet gateway tidak bisa dipasang ke subnet secara langsung, dan ENI Glue tidak punya IP publik. VPC kedua dengan peering menambah kompleksitas tanpa alasan. Ingat: Glue JDBC connection di VPC → self-referencing SG rule + akses S3 (gateway endpoint atau NAT).","r":["Salah — Membuka database ke internet melanggar praktik keamanan dan tidak menyelesaikan kebutuhan akses Glue ke S3.","Benar — Glue mewajibkan self-referencing inbound rule agar ENI-nya bisa saling berkomunikasi.","Benar — Tanpa NAT, S3 gateway endpoint memberi Glue akses ke S3 dari subnet privat.","Salah — Internet gateway tidak dipasang per subnet dan ENI Glue tidak punya IP publik, jadi ini tidak bekerja.","Salah — VPC tambahan dan peering menambah kompleksitas dan tetap tidak memenuhi syarat SG dan akses S3."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue connection gagal di VPC privat → self-referencing SG rule + S3 VPC gateway endpoint (atau NAT)."},{"id":"E2B-15","d":2,"ts":"2.2.1","t":"Firehose record format conversion with Data Catalog","q":"A company ingests JSON clickstream records with Amazon Data Firehose and wants them stored in Amazon S3 as Apache Parquet so that Amazon Athena queries are cheaper. The schema of the records is already defined as a table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. The company wants the conversion done with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Deliver the JSON files to S3 and run an hourly AWS Glue ETL job that converts the new files to Parquet.","Add an AWS Lambda transformation function to Firehose that rewrites each record as Parquet.","Enable record format conversion in Firehose, choose Parquet as the output format, and reference the Data Catalog table as the schema.","Deliver the JSON files to S3 and use Athena CTAS queries each night to convert them to Parquet."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'already defined as a table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon Data Firehose punya fitur record format conversion yang mengubah JSON menjadi Parquet atau ORC sebelum menulis ke S3; fitur ini membutuhkan skema yang diambil dari sebuah tabel di Glue Data Catalog. Jadi catalog dipakai langsung untuk menafsirkan data dari sumbernya tanpa job tambahan. Glue ETL job per jam dan Athena CTAS malam hari berfungsi, tetapi menambah job terjadwal, salinan data mentah, dan latensi. Lambda transformation mengolah batch record, tetapi menulis Parquet sendiri adalah kode kustom yang rumit dan bukan tujuan fitur itu. Ingat: Firehose JSON → Parquet/ORC → aktifkan record format conversion dengan skema dari Glue Data Catalog.","r":["Salah — Glue job terjadwal menambah pipeline kedua dan latensi, padahal Firehose bisa mengonversi langsung.","Salah — Membuat Parquet di Lambda adalah kode kustom yang rumit dan menambah biaya pemanggilan.","Benar — Record format conversion Firehose memakai skema tabel Data Catalog untuk menulis Parquet tanpa job tambahan.","Salah — CTAS malam hari menambah pekerjaan terjadwal dan menyimpan data dua kali."],"k":"Tips ujian: Firehose + 'convert to Parquet/ORC' → record format conversion + skema dari Glue Data Catalog."},{"id":"E2B-04","d":2,"ts":"2.2.2","t":"Hive metastore migration to Glue Data Catalog","q":"A company is migrating an on-premises Hadoop data lake to AWS. The on-premises Apache Hive metastore runs on a MySQL database and contains about 3,000 table definitions with partitions. After migration, Amazon Athena, AWS Glue ETL jobs, and Amazon EMR must all use the same technical catalog. The company does not want to manage any database servers for metadata. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Restore the MySQL metastore database to an Amazon EC2 instance and point Athena, AWS Glue, and EMR to it.","Migrate the Hive metastore into the AWS Glue Data Catalog by using an AWS Glue ETL job or the AWS-provided Hive metastore migration scripts.","Restore the metastore to Amazon Aurora MySQL and configure it as an external Hive metastore for every EMR cluster.","Re-create the 3,000 tables manually in Amazon Athena by running CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE statements from the Athena console."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'Athena, AWS Glue ETL jobs, and Amazon EMR must all use the same technical catalog' dan 'does not want to manage any database servers'. AWS Glue Data Catalog adalah metastore terkelola yang kompatibel dengan Hive dan dipakai bersama oleh ketiga layanan itu. AWS menyediakan skrip migrasi Hive metastore (dijalankan sebagai Glue ETL job atau langsung) yang mengekspor database, tabel dan partisi ke Data Catalog. Aurora MySQL sebagai external metastore memang terkelola, tetapi tetap sebuah database yang harus diurus, dan Athena/Glue tidak memakainya sebagai catalog bawaan. EC2 dengan MySQL melanggar syarat tanpa server. Membuat ulang 3.000 tabel secara manual rawan salah dan memakan waktu. Ingat: migrasi Hive metastore ke serverless → Glue Data Catalog.","r":["Salah — MySQL di EC2 berarti Anda mengelola server database, yang dilarang skenario.","Benar — Migrasi ke Glue Data Catalog memberi satu catalog serverless yang dipakai Athena, Glue dan EMR.","Salah — Aurora tetap database yang harus dikelola, dan hanya EMR yang memakainya sebagai external metastore.","Salah — Membuat ulang ribuan tabel dan partisi secara manual sangat lambat dan rawan kesalahan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'migrate Hive metastore' + 'no servers' + Athena/Glue/EMR → Glue Data Catalog."},{"id":"E2B-28","d":2,"ts":"2.2.6","t":"SageMaker Catalog data sources","q":"A company keeps its technical metadata in the AWS Glue Data Catalog, which crawlers update daily. The company also uses Amazon SageMaker Catalog as its business catalog. New tables and schema changes in the Glue database 'sales_curated' must appear in SageMaker Catalog every day without anyone importing them manually. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an AWS Glue data source for 'sales_curated' in the producer project, schedule it to run daily, and configure it to publish the imported assets to the catalog.","Write an AWS Lambda function that calls the Glue GetTables API and creates catalog assets through the SageMaker Catalog API each day.","Ask the producer team to re-create the assets manually in SageMaker Unified Studio after every crawler run.","Export the Glue Data Catalog to Amazon S3 each day and upload the export as a file asset in SageMaker Catalog."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: perubahan di Glue Data Catalog harus muncul di SageMaker Catalog 'every day without anyone importing them manually' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. SageMaker Catalog punya data source untuk AWS Glue (dan Redshift) di sebuah project; data source run mengimpor metadata teknis tabel ke inventory project dan bisa dijadwalkan. Dengan opsi publish otomatis, asset baru atau yang berubah langsung dipublikasikan ke catalog. Ingat bahwa asset yang diperbarui harus dipublikasikan ulang agar versi terbaru aktif, sehingga publish otomatis penting. Lambda kustom berfungsi, tetapi Anda harus memelihara kode dan logika versioning. Impor manual melanggar syarat. Ekspor ke file kehilangan struktur tabel per asset. Ingat: sinkronisasi technical catalog → business catalog → scheduled data source run.","r":["Benar — Data source Glue terjadwal dengan publish otomatis menjaga business catalog tetap sinkron tanpa kode.","Salah — Kode Lambda kustom menambah overhead pemeliharaan untuk fitur yang sudah tersedia.","Salah — Proses manual setiap hari melanggar syarat tanpa impor manual.","Salah — Ekspor ke satu file tidak membuat asset tabel yang bisa dicari dan dilanggan."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue Data Catalog → SageMaker Catalog secara otomatis → data source (Glue/Redshift) dengan jadwal + auto-publish."},{"id":"E4A-18","d":4,"ts":"4.1.5","t":"Bucket policy with aws:SourceVpce","q":"A company stores sensitive data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Applications access the bucket from a VPC through a gateway VPC endpoint (vpce-0abc1234). The security team requires that all requests to the bucket that do not come through this endpoint be denied, even if the caller has valid IAM permissions. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Add a bucket policy statement that denies all s3 actions when the aws:SourceVpce condition key does not equal vpce-0abc1234.","Add a bucket policy statement that denies all s3 actions when aws:SourceIp is not within the VPC's private CIDR range.","Attach a security group to the bucket that allows inbound traffic only from the VPC endpoint.","Configure a network ACL on the private subnets that blocks traffic to the public S3 IP ranges."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'not come through this endpoint be denied, even if the caller has valid IAM permissions'. Kebutuhan ini harus ditegakkan di resource, yaitu bucket policy dengan Deny eksplisit, karena explicit deny mengalahkan Allow apa pun di IAM. Kondisi aws:SourceVpce (StringNotEquals) memastikan hanya request lewat endpoint tertentu yang lolos. aws:SourceIp tidak bisa dipakai untuk IP privat ketika request lewat VPC endpoint, sehingga kondisi itu akan memblokir semua atau tidak bekerja sesuai harapan. S3 bucket tidak bisa diberi security group. Network ACL di subnet hanya memengaruhi traffic dari subnet itu, tidak memblokir akses dari luar VPC. Aturan umum: 'only via VPC endpoint' → bucket policy Deny dengan aws:SourceVpce atau aws:SourceVpc.","r":["Benar — Explicit deny dengan aws:SourceVpce di bucket policy memblokir semua akses yang tidak melewati endpoint tersebut.","Salah — aws:SourceIp tidak berisi IP privat untuk request yang lewat VPC endpoint, sehingga kondisi ini tidak bisa dipakai untuk tujuan ini.","Salah — Security group tidak dapat dipasang pada S3 bucket.","Salah — Network ACL hanya mengatur traffic dari subnet tersebut dan tidak mencegah akses dari jaringan lain."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'access bucket only through VPC endpoint' → bucket policy Deny + aws:SourceVpce (bukan aws:SourceIp)."},{"id":"E1C-24","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Distributed Map concurrency control","q":"A Step Functions Distributed Map state invokes an AWS Lambda function that writes each item to an Amazon DynamoDB table with provisioned capacity. During large runs, many child executions fail with ProvisionedThroughputExceededException and the Map Run exceeds its tolerated failure threshold. Which combination of actions will make the workflow MORE resilient? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Set MaxConcurrency on the Distributed Map state to limit the number of parallel child executions.","Convert the Distributed Map state to a Parallel state.","Add a Retry on the Lambda task for the throttling error with exponential backoff and jitter.","Remove the tolerated failure threshold so that any failure stops the Map Run immediately.","Increase the Lambda function memory to speed up each write."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Akar masalahnya adalah terlalu banyak penulisan paralel yang melampaui kapasitas DynamoDB, dengan tujuan workflow 'MORE resilient'. MaxConcurrency membatasi jumlah child execution paralel sehingga laju tulis berada dalam kapasitas tabel. Retry dengan exponential backoff dan jitter memungkinkan item yang sempat di-throttle berhasil pada percobaan berikutnya tanpa serbuan serentak. Distractor terdekat adalah menambah memori Lambda: setiap tulis menjadi lebih cepat, sehingga laju permintaan justru naik dan throttling bisa memburuk. Parallel state tidak ditujukan untuk iterasi data dinamis. Menghapus tolerated failure threshold membuat pipeline lebih rapuh. Aturan umum: throttling downstream akibat fan-out → batasi konkurensi + retry dengan backoff dan jitter.","r":["Benar — Membatasi konkurensi menjaga laju tulis di bawah kapasitas DynamoDB.","Salah — Parallel state untuk cabang tetap, bukan pengganti Map untuk item dinamis.","Benar — Retry dengan backoff dan jitter memulihkan kegagalan throttling sementara.","Salah — Membuat Map Run gagal lebih cepat, bukan lebih tangguh.","Salah — Tulis lebih cepat meningkatkan laju permintaan dan tidak mengatasi throttling."],"k":"Tips ujian: fan-out membuat downstream throttling → MaxConcurrency + Retry backoff/jitter."},{"id":"E1C-04","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"Glue workflow EventBridge event batching","q":"Partner systems upload small CSV files to an Amazon S3 prefix throughout the day. An AWS Glue workflow processes the files. To reduce the number of workflow runs, the workflow must start when 100 new files have arrived or 15 minutes after the first new file arrives, whichever happens first. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Configure S3 Event Notifications to invoke an AWS Lambda function that counts files in Amazon DynamoDB and starts the workflow when the count reaches 100 or the oldest file is 15 minutes old.","Add a scheduled trigger to the Glue workflow that runs every 15 minutes.","Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the bucket, create an EventBridge rule for Object Created events on the prefix that targets the Glue workflow, and configure the workflow's event trigger with a batch size of 100 and a batch window of 900 seconds.","Configure an AWS Glue crawler with S3 event mode and start the workflow from the crawler on every run."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya '100 new files' atau '15 minutes after the first new file', mana yang lebih dulu, dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Glue workflow mendukung trigger berbasis event EventBridge dengan batching condition: batch size (1–100 event) dan batch window (1–900 detik, dimulai sejak event pertama). Kondisi yang terpenuhi lebih dulu yang memulai workflow, persis sesuai kebutuhan, tanpa kode. Distractor terdekat adalah Lambda + DynamoDB counter: berfungsi, tetapi Anda harus membangun dan memelihara logika penghitungan dan timer sendiri. Scheduled trigger tiap 15 menit tidak bereaksi terhadap jumlah file dan tetap jalan walau tidak ada file baru. Aturan umum: 'jalankan Glue workflow setelah N event atau T detik' → EventBridge event trigger dengan batch size dan batch window.","r":["Salah — Bisa bekerja, tetapi menambah kode kustom, tabel DynamoDB, dan logika timer yang harus dipelihara.","Salah — Jadwal tetap tidak merespons 100 file, dan menjalankan workflow walaupun tidak ada data baru.","Benar — Event trigger Glue mendukung batch size 100 dan batch window maksimum 900 detik; mana yang lebih dulu memulai workflow, tanpa kode kustom.","Salah — Crawler tidak menghitung batch file untuk memulai workflow dan tidak memberi kondisi '100 file atau 15 menit'."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue workflow 'N events OR T seconds' → EventBridge trigger dengan batch size (maks 100) dan batch window (maks 900 detik)."},{"id":"E2C-39","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Avro vs Parquet by data zone","q":"A company streams clickstream records from Amazon MSK into an Amazon S3 raw zone. Producers evolve the record schema frequently, and records are written one at a time. A nightly AWS Glue job then builds a curated zone that analysts query with Amazon Athena, mostly aggregating a few columns. Which file format choice is MOST appropriate for each zone?","o":["Use CSV in the raw zone and JSON in the curated zone.","Use Apache Parquet in both zones.","Use Apache Avro in the raw zone and Apache Parquet in the curated zone.","Use Apache Parquet in the raw zone and Apache Avro in the curated zone."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah raw zone dengan 'schema frequently' berubah dan 'written one at a time', sedangkan curated zone dipakai untuk 'aggregating a few columns'. Apache Avro adalah format row-based dengan schema yang tertanam dan dukungan schema evolution yang kuat, sehingga cocok untuk penulisan record per record dari streaming dan integrasi dengan schema registry. Apache Parquet adalah format kolumnar yang efisien untuk query analitik yang membaca sebagian kolom dan melakukan agregasi. Parquet di raw zone kurang cocok untuk penulisan per record karena format kolumnar optimal ditulis dalam batch besar. Avro di curated zone membuat Athena membaca seluruh baris. CSV dan JSON tidak memiliki tipe data kuat dan kurang efisien untuk analitik. Aturan umum: row-based (Avro) untuk ingest/streaming dan schema evolution; kolumnar (Parquet/ORC) untuk analitik.","r":["Salah — CSV tidak menyimpan schema dan JSON di curated zone tidak efisien untuk analitik kolom.","Salah — Parquet tidak ideal untuk penulisan record per record dari streaming di raw zone.","Benar — Avro cocok untuk ingest streaming dengan schema evolution, Parquet cocok untuk query analitik.","Salah — Urutannya terbalik; Avro row-based di curated zone membuat query analitik membaca seluruh baris."],"k":"Tips ujian: streaming/write-heavy + schema evolution → Avro; analitik kolom → Parquet/ORC."},{"id":"E1A-04","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"DynamoDB Streams view types","q":"A company stores customer profiles in an Amazon DynamoDB table. A downstream audit process must receive every change to the table and must be able to compare the value of each item before and after the modification. Which configuration should a data engineer use?","o":["Enable DynamoDB Streams with the KEYS_ONLY view type and query the table for the current item.","Enable DynamoDB Streams with the NEW_IMAGE view type.","Enable DynamoDB Streams with the NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES view type and process the stream records with AWS Lambda.","Schedule a daily DynamoDB export to Amazon S3 and compare consecutive exports."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'every change' dan 'compare the value of each item before and after the modification'. DynamoDB Streams menangkap setiap perubahan item, dan stream view type NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES menyertakan isi item sebelum dan sesudah perubahan dalam satu record. Lambda bisa membaca stream ini secara otomatis melalui event source mapping. Distraktor terdekat adalah NEW_IMAGE, tetapi itu hanya berisi nilai sesudah perubahan sehingga perbandingan tidak mungkin. KEYS_ONLY hanya memberikan key, dan query ke tabel hanya mendapatkan nilai terkini, bukan nilai lama. Export harian kehilangan perubahan intra-hari. Aturan umum: butuh before/after image → NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES.","r":["Salah — KEYS_ONLY hanya berisi atribut key; nilai lama tidak bisa direkonstruksi dari tabel.","Salah — NEW_IMAGE hanya berisi nilai setelah perubahan, tidak ada nilai sebelumnya.","Benar — NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES memuat item sebelum dan sesudah perubahan, dan Lambda dapat memprosesnya per perubahan.","Salah — Export harian tidak menangkap setiap perubahan (beberapa update di hari yang sama akan hilang)."],"k":"'before and after' → DynamoDB Streams NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES."},{"id":"E2A-51","d":2,"ts":"2.1.7","t":"Apache Iceberg for data lakes","q":"A company's data lake in Amazon S3 stores customer records as Parquet files in Hive-style partitions. To meet privacy regulations, the company must delete or update individual customer records on request, readers must never see partially written results, and auditors want to query the table as it existed at earlier points in time. Analysts use Amazon Athena. Which approach meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Keep the Hive-style Parquet tables and rewrite each affected partition with an AWS Glue job when a request arrives.","Convert the data to Apache Iceberg tables registered in the AWS Glue Data Catalog and use Athena DELETE, UPDATE, and time travel queries.","Move the customer records to Amazon DynamoDB and use S3 Versioning for history.","Store each customer's data in a separate S3 prefix and delete the prefix on request."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'delete or update individual customer records', 'never see partially written results' (ACID), dan 'query the table as it existed at earlier points in time' (time travel), dengan Athena sebagai engine. Apache Iceberg adalah open table format yang menambahkan transaksi ACID, operasi row-level (DELETE, UPDATE, MERGE INTO), snapshot untuk time travel, serta schema dan partition evolution di atas file Parquet di S3; Athena mendukung semua operasi ini langsung pada tabel Iceberg di Glue Data Catalog. Distraktor terdekat adalah menulis ulang partisi dengan Glue: hasil akhirnya bisa benar, tetapi pembaca dapat melihat data setengah jadi, tidak ada time travel, dan perlu kode kustom. DynamoDB tidak cocok untuk analitik Athena. Prefix per pelanggan tidak skalabel dan tidak memberi ACID. Aturan umum: data lake butuh ACID + row-level update/delete + time travel → Apache Iceberg.","r":["Salah — Penulisan ulang partisi tidak atomik bagi pembaca, tidak memberi time travel, dan membutuhkan kode kustom.","Benar — Tabel Iceberg memberi ACID, DELETE/UPDATE tingkat baris, dan time travel yang didukung langsung oleh Athena.","Salah — DynamoDB tidak sesuai untuk query analitik Athena, dan S3 Versioning tidak memberi time travel tingkat tabel.","Salah — Jutaan prefix per pelanggan tidak efisien untuk analitik dan tidak memberikan transaksi ACID."],"k":"ACID + row-level deletes (GDPR) + time travel on S3 data lake → Apache Iceberg tables."},{"id":"E2A-16","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"RDS read replicas vs Multi-AZ","q":"An Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance supports an order-processing application. Analysts run heavy reporting queries every hour, which cause high CPU and slow down order transactions. The reports can tolerate data that is a few seconds old. Which solution resolves the issue with the LEAST impact on the application?","o":["Create a read replica of the DB instance and direct the reporting queries to the replica endpoint.","Convert the instance to a Multi-AZ DB instance deployment and run the reports on the standby instance.","Scale the DB instance to a larger instance class and keep running the reports on the primary.","Schedule the reports to run only at night on the primary instance."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah beban baca berat dari 'reporting queries' yang mengganggu transaksi dan laporan yang 'can tolerate data that is a few seconds old'. Read replica RDS menerima replikasi asinkron dari primary dan dapat melayani query read-only, sehingga beban laporan dipindahkan dari primary; lag beberapa detik sesuai toleransi. Distraktor terdekat adalah Multi-AZ DB instance deployment: standby di deployment ini hanya untuk failover dan tidak bisa menerima traffic baca. Menaikkan ukuran instance hanya menunda masalah dan menambah biaya, sementara menjadwalkan laporan di malam hari mengubah kebutuhan bisnis (laporan per jam). Aturan umum: memisahkan beban baca/analitik dari OLTP di RDS → read replica; Multi-AZ instance standby = HA, bukan scaling baca.","r":["Benar — Read replica memindahkan beban query laporan dari primary dan lag replikasi beberapa detik dapat diterima.","Salah — Standby pada Multi-AZ DB instance deployment tidak dapat dipakai untuk membaca; fungsinya hanya failover.","Salah — Instance lebih besar menambah biaya dan laporan tetap bersaing dengan transaksi di primary.","Salah — Menggeser jadwal ke malam hari melanggar kebutuhan laporan setiap jam."],"k":"Offload read/reporting from RDS primary → read replica; Multi-AZ instance standby tidak melayani read."},{"id":"E2C-30","d":2,"ts":"2.4.4","t":"Impact analysis with data and ML lineage","q":"A company discovers that a corrupted batch was written into a curated customer table three days ago. The data engineer must quickly determine (1) which downstream data assets consumed the table and (2) which machine learning models were trained on datasets derived from it, so those models can be retrained. Which TWO AWS capabilities should the data engineer use? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Amazon SageMaker Catalog data lineage to trace downstream data assets of the curated table.","Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking to find training jobs and model versions associated with the affected dataset artifacts.","AWS Config to view configuration changes on the S3 bucket.","Amazon Macie to scan the corrupted batch for sensitive data.","S3 Object Lock to make the corrupted objects immutable."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah dua pertanyaan dampak: aset data downstream dan model ML yang dilatih dari data turunan. SageMaker Catalog data lineage menampilkan graph upstream/downstream antar aset data (misalnya tabel hasil job Glue atau Redshift), sehingga dapat menjawab pertanyaan pertama. SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking menghubungkan artifact dataset dengan training job dan model, sehingga dapat menjawab model mana yang perlu dilatih ulang. AWS Config melacak perubahan konfigurasi resource, bukan aliran data. Macie mendeteksi data sensitif, bukan dampak data korup. Object Lock mencegah penghapusan/perubahan objek, yang justru tidak membantu analisis dampak. Aturan umum: impact analysis data → SageMaker Catalog lineage; impact analysis model → ML Lineage Tracking.","r":["Benar — Lineage SageMaker Catalog menunjukkan aset data downstream yang mengonsumsi tabel yang korup.","Benar — ML Lineage Tracking menghubungkan dataset artifact dengan training job dan model yang terdampak.","Salah — AWS Config mencatat perubahan konfigurasi resource, bukan aliran data antar dataset.","Salah — Macie mendeteksi data sensitif, tidak membantu menelusuri dampak downstream.","Salah — Object Lock membuat objek immutable dan tidak memberikan informasi lineage."],"k":"Tips ujian: dampak ke aset data → SageMaker Catalog lineage; dampak ke model ML → SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking."},{"id":"E2C-05","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"DynamoDB GSI vs LSI","q":"An existing Amazon DynamoDB table uses device_id as the partition key and reading_time as the sort key. Six months after launch, the operations team needs a new access pattern: query all readings that have a specific alarm_status, sorted by reading_time, across all devices. The table must remain online. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create a local secondary index (LSI) with alarm_status as the sort key.","Create a global secondary index (GSI) with alarm_status as the partition key and reading_time as the sort key.","Run a periodic Scan with a filter expression on alarm_status and cache the result in Amazon ElastiCache.","Recreate the table with alarm_status as the partition key and migrate all items with AWS DMS."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah access pattern baru 'across all devices' pada tabel yang sudah berjalan dan 'must remain online'. Global secondary index (GSI) dapat ditambahkan kapan saja pada tabel yang sudah ada, dan GSI boleh memiliki partition key yang berbeda dari tabel dasar (alarm_status) dengan sort key reading_time. Local secondary index (LSI) hanya bisa dibuat saat tabel dibuat dan harus memakai partition key yang sama (device_id), sehingga tidak bisa melakukan query lintas device. Scan berkala mahal dan tidak memberikan data real time. Membuat ulang tabel dan migrasi adalah overhead besar dan berisiko downtime. Aturan umum: access pattern baru dengan partition key berbeda → GSI; LSI hanya untuk sort key alternatif dengan partition key yang sama dan harus didefinisikan saat create table.","r":["Salah — LSI hanya dapat dibuat saat pembuatan tabel dan tetap memakai partition key device_id, jadi tidak bisa query lintas device.","Benar — GSI bisa ditambahkan online dengan partition key alarm_status dan sort key reading_time untuk access pattern baru.","Salah — Scan berkala membaca seluruh tabel, mahal, dan hasilnya tidak selalu terbaru.","Salah — Membuat ulang tabel dan migrasi data menambah overhead besar padahal GSI sudah cukup."],"k":"Tips ujian: access pattern baru setelah tabel jadi / partition key berbeda → GSI (LSI hanya saat create table)."},{"id":"E3A-62","d":3,"ts":"3.2.5","t":"Athena on-demand vs provisioned capacity","q":"A company uses Amazon Athena for hundreds of scheduled reporting queries that run throughout the business day. The query volume is high and predictable. During peak hours, queries sometimes wait in a queue because of shared service capacity, and the finance team wants a predictable monthly cost instead of a per-TB-scanned bill. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create Athena capacity reservations with a fixed number of DPUs and assign the reporting workgroup to the reservation.","Enable query result reuse on all reporting queries.","Move the queries to Athena notebooks with the Apache Spark engine.","Increase the per-query data usage control limit in the workgroup."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'high and predictable volume', 'queries wait in a queue because of shared capacity', dan 'predictable monthly cost instead of per-TB-scanned'. Athena provisioned capacity (capacity reservations) memungkinkan Anda mereservasi sejumlah DPU khusus untuk satu atau beberapa workgroup. Query di workgroup tersebut berjalan di kapasitas dedicated sehingga tidak bersaing dengan kapasitas bersama dan tidak dihitung ke kuota query DDL/DML akun, dan biayanya berdasarkan DPU yang direservasi per jam, bukan data yang dipindai. Query result reuse membantu untuk query yang identik, tetapi tidak menjamin kapasitas maupun mengubah model biaya. Notebook Spark untuk eksplorasi PySpark, bukan query laporan SQL. Data usage control hanya membatasi data yang dipindai per query. Aturan umum: Athena on-demand (per TB) untuk beban sporadis; capacity reservations untuk beban SQL yang tinggi, stabil, dan butuh kapasitas terjamin.","r":["Benar — Capacity reservations memberi kapasitas DPU khusus dan biaya yang dapat diprediksi untuk beban stabil.","Salah — Result reuse tidak menjamin kapasitas dan tidak mengubah model penagihan.","Salah — Notebook Spark tidak cocok untuk query laporan SQL terjadwal.","Salah — Batas data per query tidak menambah kapasitas atau membuat biaya lebih dapat diprediksi."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena 'predictable cost + dedicated capacity untuk beban tinggi' → capacity reservations (provisioned DPUs)."},{"id":"E1A-35","d":1,"ts":"1.1.5","t":"EventBridge Scheduler one-time schedules","q":"A company lets each of its 3,000 enterprise customers request a one-off historical data export. When a customer submits a request, the customer chooses a future date and time, and an AWS Step Functions state machine that builds the export must start exactly once at that time. The company wants a serverless solution with the LEAST operational overhead and does not want thousands of finished schedules to accumulate. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with a cron expression for each customer request.","Run an AWS Lambda function every minute that queries a DynamoDB table of requests and starts the state machine when a request is due.","For each request, create an Amazon EventBridge Scheduler one-time schedule with an at() expression that targets the Step Functions state machine.","Use an Amazon SQS delay queue to hold each request until its scheduled time.","Configure the schedules to be deleted automatically after completion by setting ActionAfterCompletion to DELETE."],"a":[2,4],"e":"Kata kunci: setiap permintaan berjalan 'exactly once' pada waktu yang dipilih pelanggan, 'serverless', 'LEAST operational overhead', dan jadwal yang sudah selesai tidak boleh menumpuk. Amazon EventBridge Scheduler mendukung one-time schedule dengan ekspresi at() (beserta zona waktu) yang memanggil target satu kali, termasuk langsung memulai eksekusi Step Functions. Dengan ActionAfterCompletion = DELETE, Scheduler menghapus schedule secara otomatis setelah invocation terakhirnya, sehingga ribuan jadwal yang selesai tidak perlu dibersihkan manual. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda yang berjalan tiap menit dan membaca tabel permintaan: berfungsi, tetapi berupa kode kustom, polling terus-menerus, dan butuh logika anti-duplikasi sendiri. EventBridge rule berbasis cron dirancang untuk jadwal berulang dan dibatasi kuota jumlah rule per event bus, sehingga tidak cocok untuk ribuan jadwal sekali jalan. SQS delay queue hanya bisa menunda pesan maksimum 15 menit, jauh dari tanggal yang bisa berhari-hari ke depan. Aturan umum: jadwal sekali jalan dalam jumlah besar = EventBridge Scheduler one-time schedule (at()) + hapus otomatis setelah selesai.","r":["Salah — Rule cron ditujukan untuk jadwal berulang, dibatasi kuota rule per bus, dan harus dihapus manual setelah dipakai.","Salah — Polling tiap menit adalah kode kustom yang terus berjalan dan butuh logika sendiri agar tiap permintaan hanya dieksekusi sekali.","Benar — One-time schedule dengan at() memanggil state machine satu kali pada waktu yang ditentukan, tanpa server.","Salah — Delay SQS maksimum 15 menit, tidak bisa menahan permintaan berhari-hari.","Benar — ActionAfterCompletion = DELETE menghapus schedule otomatis setelah invocation terakhir sehingga jadwal tidak menumpuk."],"k":"Ribuan jadwal sekali jalan → EventBridge Scheduler one-time schedule (at()) + ActionAfterCompletion DELETE."},{"id":"E1C-29","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions versions and aliases","q":"A data team maintains a production AWS Step Functions state machine that is started thousands of times a day by an Amazon EventBridge rule. The team has a new version of the workflow definition and wants to send 10% of new executions to it, monitor errors, and quickly shift back if needed, without changing the EventBridge rule each time. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a second state machine and add a second EventBridge rule that sends 10% of events to it.","Update the existing state machine definition in place and roll back by editing the definition if errors increase.","Publish the new definition as a state machine version, and point the EventBridge rule at an alias whose routing configuration sends 90% of executions to the current version and 10% to the new version.","Use an Express workflow for the new definition and a Standard workflow for the old one."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: kirim '10% of new executions' ke definisi baru, pantau, dan 'shift back' dengan cepat 'without changing the EventBridge rule'. Step Functions mendukung versions (snapshot definisi yang immutable) dan aliases; alias dapat merutekan eksekusi ke hingga dua versi dengan bobot tertentu. Karena rule EventBridge menunjuk ke ARN alias, pergeseran bobot atau rollback cukup dilakukan dengan memperbarui alias. Distractor terdekat adalah state machine kedua dengan rule kedua: rule EventBridge tidak bisa membagi persentase event secara bawaan, dan perubahan harus dilakukan di beberapa tempat. Update in place tidak memberi canary dan rollback lambat serta rawan kesalahan. Mencampur Express dan Standard mengubah semantik eksekusi. Aturan umum: deployment bertahap state machine → versions + alias routing.","r":["Salah — Rule EventBridge tidak membagi trafik berdasarkan persentase, dan pengelolaannya lebih rumit.","Salah — Tidak ada canary; semua eksekusi langsung memakai definisi baru.","Benar — Alias dengan routing berbobot ke dua versi memungkinkan canary 10% dan rollback cepat tanpa mengubah rule.","Salah — Tipe workflow berbeda tidak menyelesaikan pembagian trafik dan mengubah semantik eksekusi."],"k":"Tips ujian: canary/rollback untuk state machine → Step Functions versions + aliases."},{"id":"E2B-39","d":2,"ts":"2.3.2","t":"S3 One Zone-IA for reproducible data","q":"A data pipeline stores intermediate Parquet files in Amazon S3. The files are read for about 2 months during reprocessing and are rarely accessed afterward. They can be regenerated from the raw data in another bucket at any time if they are lost. The company wants to minimize the storage cost of these intermediate files after 30 days while keeping millisecond access. Which storage class should the Lifecycle rule transition the files to?","o":["S3 Standard-IA","S3 Glacier Deep Archive","S3 One Zone-IA","S3 Express One Zone"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'can be regenerated ... if they are lost', 'rarely accessed' dan 'millisecond access'. S3 One Zone-IA menyimpan data di satu Availability Zone dengan harga sekitar 20% lebih murah daripada Standard-IA dan tetap memberi akses milidetik. Risikonya adalah kehilangan data jika AZ tersebut rusak, tetapi itu dapat diterima karena file bisa dibuat ulang dari data mentah. Standard-IA lebih tahan, tetapi lebih mahal tanpa manfaat tambahan untuk data yang bisa diregenerasi. Deep Archive tidak memberi akses milidetik. S3 Express One Zone adalah kelas berperforma tinggi dengan harga penyimpanan lebih mahal, bukan untuk data dingin. Ingat: data yang bisa dibuat ulang + jarang diakses → One Zone-IA.","r":["Salah — Standard-IA tahan multi-AZ tetapi lebih mahal; ketahanan itu tidak diperlukan untuk data yang bisa diregenerasi.","Salah — Deep Archive butuh berjam-jam untuk pengambilan, sehingga melanggar syarat akses milidetik.","Benar — One Zone-IA paling murah untuk data jarang diakses yang bisa dibuat ulang, dengan akses milidetik.","Salah — Express One Zone dirancang untuk latensi sangat rendah dengan harga penyimpanan tinggi, bukan untuk data dingin."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'reproducible / can be recreated' + infrequent → S3 One Zone-IA."},{"id":"E4B-29","d":4,"ts":"4.4.2","t":"Lambda logging to CloudWatch Logs","q":"A data engineer deploys a new AWS Lambda function that transforms files as part of a data pipeline. The function runs successfully, but no log group or log events appear in Amazon CloudWatch Logs for the function. Other Lambda functions in the account log normally. What is the MOST likely cause?","o":["CloudTrail data events for Lambda are not enabled in the account.","The function's timeout is shorter than the CloudWatch Logs delivery interval.","The function's execution role does not have the logs:CreateLogGroup, logs:CreateLogStream, and logs:PutLogEvents permissions, such as those in the AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole managed policy.","The CloudWatch agent is not installed in the Lambda execution environment."],"a":[2],"e":"Petunjuk kuncinya: fungsi berjalan normal tetapi 'no log group or log events appear', sementara fungsi lain log dengan normal. Lambda mengirim output log (stdout/stderr dan logger) ke CloudWatch Logs secara otomatis, tetapi memakai izin execution role fungsi; tanpa logs:CreateLogGroup, logs:CreateLogStream, dan logs:PutLogEvents (misalnya dari managed policy AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole) log tidak akan tertulis. Distraktor terdekat adalah CloudWatch agent: agent dibutuhkan untuk EC2/on-premises, bukan Lambda yang sudah terintegrasi bawaan. CloudTrail data events untuk Lambda mencatat invocation API, bukan log aplikasi fungsi. Timeout tidak berhubungan dengan pembuatan log group. Aturan umum: log Lambda tidak muncul → periksa izin CloudWatch Logs pada execution role.","r":["Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API Invoke, bukan log aplikasi di dalam fungsi.","Salah — Tidak ada interval pengiriman yang membuat log hilang karena timeout; fungsi bahkan berjalan sukses.","Benar — Tanpa izin CloudWatch Logs di execution role, Lambda tidak dapat membuat log group/stream dan menulis event.","Salah — Lambda terintegrasi langsung dengan CloudWatch Logs tanpa agent."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Lambda logs missing' → execution role kurang izin logs:* (AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole)."},{"id":"E3B-53","d":3,"ts":"3.4.3","t":"Investigating consistency with DataBrew profiles","q":"A data analyst notices that a sales report shows separate rows for 'US', 'USA', 'United States', and 'u.s.' in the country column. The analyst needs to quickly investigate how many distinct variants exist and how often each appears across a 30-column dataset in Amazon S3, without writing code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler on the dataset and review the table schema.","Run an AWS Glue DataBrew profile job on the dataset and review the column statistics, including distinct values and value distribution for the country column.","Enable S3 Inventory on the bucket.","Create a CloudWatch Logs Insights query on the dataset."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'investigate how many distinct variants exist and how often each appears' dan 'without writing code'. DataBrew profile job menghasilkan data profile per kolom: jumlah nilai distinct, nilai yang paling sering muncul (value distribution), missing values, duplicate, dan outlier, sehingga inkonsistensi seperti variasi penulisan negara langsung terlihat secara visual. Distraktor terdekat adalah crawler: hanya menyimpulkan skema dan tipe data, tidak menganalisis isi nilai. S3 Inventory mendaftar objek, bukan isi data. Logs Insights hanya untuk log group. Setelah investigasi, perbaikan bisa dilakukan dengan recipe (misalnya replace values). Aturan: investigasi konsistensi isi data tanpa kode → DataBrew profile.","r":["Salah — Crawler hanya menangkap skema, bukan distribusi nilai dalam kolom.","Benar — Profile DataBrew menampilkan nilai distinct dan distribusinya sehingga variasi penulisan mudah diidentifikasi.","Salah — S3 Inventory mencantumkan metadata objek, bukan isi kolom.","Salah — Logs Insights meng-query log CloudWatch, bukan dataset di S3."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'investigate data consistency / distinct values without code' → DataBrew profile job."},{"id":"E1A-61","d":1,"ts":"1.1.10","t":"Fan-out with multiple Firehose streams","q":"An Amazon Kinesis data stream carries application events. The company wants the same events delivered to an Amazon S3 data lake and to an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain for search, with the LEAST operational overhead and without writing consumer code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create one Amazon Data Firehose stream with the Kinesis data stream as the source and configure both Amazon S3 and OpenSearch Service as destinations.","Create two Amazon Data Firehose streams, each with the Kinesis data stream as its source, one delivering to Amazon S3 and the other to OpenSearch Service.","Write a Kinesis Client Library application on Amazon EC2 that writes each record to both destinations.","Configure S3 Event Notifications on the data lake bucket to index each new object into OpenSearch Service with a Lambda function."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: data yang sama ke 'Amazon S3' dan 'OpenSearch Service', 'LEAST operational overhead', 'without writing consumer code'. Sebuah Firehose stream hanya memiliki satu destination (backup S3 pada destination OpenSearch adalah fitur cadangan, bukan pengganti data lake yang dirancang terpisah). Karena Kinesis Data Streams mendukung banyak consumer, dua Firehose stream dapat membaca stream yang sama secara independen, masing-masing mengirim ke satu destination: ini pola fan-out tanpa kode. Distraktor terdekat adalah satu Firehose dengan dua destination: konfigurasi seperti itu tidak didukung. Aplikasi KCL di EC2 adalah kode kustom dan server. Pipeline S3 → Lambda → OpenSearch menambah kode dan latensi. Aturan umum: fan-out KDS ke beberapa tujuan managed = beberapa Firehose stream dengan sumber KDS yang sama.","r":["Salah — Satu Firehose stream hanya mendukung satu destination.","Benar — Dua Firehose stream membaca KDS yang sama secara independen dan masing-masing mengirim ke satu tujuan tanpa kode.","Salah — Aplikasi KCL di EC2 adalah kode kustom dan menambah pengelolaan server.","Salah — Menambah kode Lambda dan latensi, serta bergantung pada data lake terlebih dahulu."],"k":"KDS → beberapa tujuan tanpa kode → satu Firehose stream per tujuan (fan-out)."},{"id":"E2A-08","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"S3 data lake with Lake Formation","q":"A company is building a central data lake for 40 TB of raw and curated data in Parquet format. Data is queried occasionally by Amazon Athena and Amazon Redshift Spectrum. The marketing team must see only non-PII columns of the customer table, while the finance team can see all columns. The solution must be cost-effective and centrally governed. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Load all 40 TB into an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster and create a separate view for each team.","Store the data in Amazon S3 and catalog it in the AWS Glue Data Catalog.","Register the S3 locations with AWS Lake Formation and grant column-level permissions to each team.","Write S3 bucket policies that deny the marketing team access to the PII columns inside the Parquet files.","Store the customer table in Amazon DynamoDB and use IAM condition keys to hide PII attributes."],"a":[1,2],"e":"Persyaratan kunci: data lake 40 TB yang 'queried occasionally', akses berbeda per kolom ('non-PII columns'), 'cost-effective', dan 'centrally governed'. Amazon S3 adalah storage paling murah untuk data lake dan Glue Data Catalog menyediakan metadata yang dipakai Athena dan Redshift Spectrum. AWS Lake Formation menambahkan izin terpusat tingkat database, tabel, kolom, bahkan baris, yang diterapkan konsisten oleh Athena dan Redshift Spectrum. Distraktor terdekat adalah memuat semua data ke Redshift provisioned lalu membuat view: kontrol akses bisa dicapai, tetapi membayar cluster untuk data yang jarang di-query tidak hemat biaya. S3 bucket policy bekerja di level object/prefix, bukan kolom di dalam file Parquet. Aturan umum: data lake murah di S3 + Glue Data Catalog, dan izin granular (kolom/baris) terpusat → Lake Formation.","r":["Salah — Cluster Redshift yang selalu menyala untuk data yang jarang di-query mahal, dan pengelolaan view per tim menambah overhead.","Benar — S3 adalah storage data lake berbiaya rendah dan Glue Data Catalog menyediakan skema bagi Athena dan Redshift Spectrum.","Benar — Lake Formation memberi kontrol akses terpusat hingga level kolom yang dihormati oleh Athena dan Redshift Spectrum.","Salah — Bucket policy tidak dapat membatasi kolom di dalam file; hanya object atau prefix.","Salah — Memindahkan tabel ke DynamoDB merusak pola query analitik SQL dan tidak sesuai untuk data lake."],"k":"Column-level access di data lake S3 → Lake Formation permissions; bucket policy tidak bisa level kolom."},{"id":"E1B-50","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Managed Service for Apache Flink scaling","q":"An Apache Flink application on Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink reads from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. The application is the only consumer of the stream. During peak hours, the millisBehindLatest metric keeps increasing, CPU utilization of the application is near 100%, and the Flink dashboard shows backpressure on the processing operators. Which action will resolve the issue?","o":["Enable enhanced fan-out for the application's Kinesis consumer.","Increase the parallelism of the Flink application (or enable automatic scaling) so that more KPUs process the data.","Reduce the data retention period of the Kinesis data stream.","Increase the checkpoint interval from 1 minute to 30 minutes."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejala kuncinya adalah 'millisBehindLatest keeps increasing', 'CPU utilization ... near 100%', dan 'backpressure on the processing operators', yang menunjukkan bottleneck ada pada kapasitas pemrosesan aplikasi, bukan pada pembacaan stream. Menaikkan parallelism (atau mengaktifkan automatic scaling) menambah KPU dan subtask sehingga throughput pemrosesan meningkat dan lag berkurang. Enhanced fan-out adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi fitur itu mengatasi persaingan throughput baca antar beberapa konsumen, padahal aplikasi ini satu-satunya konsumen dan masalahnya CPU. Mengurangi retention justru berisiko kehilangan data yang belum diproses. Memperpanjang interval checkpoint sedikit mengurangi overhead, tetapi tidak mengatasi CPU yang jenuh dan memperpanjang waktu pemulihan. Aturan umum: lag + CPU tinggi + backpressure di Flink → tambah parallelism/KPU.","r":["Salah — Enhanced fan-out membantu jika ada banyak konsumen yang berbagi throughput baca, bukan saat CPU jenuh.","Benar — Parallelism lebih tinggi menambah kapasitas pemrosesan sehingga lag menurun.","Salah — Retention yang lebih pendek berisiko kehilangan data yang tertinggal.","Salah — Tidak mengatasi CPU jenuh dan memperlambat pemulihan setelah kegagalan."],"k":"Tips ujian: Flink 'millisBehindLatest naik + CPU tinggi + backpressure' → scale parallelism/KPU (autoscaling)."},{"id":"E3A-05","d":3,"ts":"3.1.2","t":"Troubleshooting MWAA DAG parsing","q":"A data engineer uploads a new DAG file to the dags folder of an Amazon MWAA environment's S3 bucket. After 15 minutes, the DAG still does not appear in the Apache Airflow UI, while other DAGs work normally. CloudWatch logging is enabled for the environment. What should the data engineer do FIRST to find the cause?","o":["Review the DAG processing logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs for import or syntax errors in the new DAG file.","Upgrade the environment class from mw1.small to mw1.large and wait for the update to complete.","Search AWS CloudTrail for the PutObject event of the DAG file.","Delete and re-create the MWAA environment so that all DAGs are reloaded."],"a":[0],"e":"Gejalanya: satu DAG baru 'does not appear in the Airflow UI', sedangkan DAG lain normal. Penyebab paling umum adalah error saat scheduler mem-parse file DAG, misalnya syntax error atau import modul yang belum ada di requirements.txt. MWAA dapat mengirim beberapa jenis log ke CloudWatch Logs, termasuk DAG processing logs, scheduler logs, task logs, worker logs, dan web server logs. DAG processing logs menunjukkan traceback error parsing untuk file tertentu, jadi itu langkah pertama yang tepat. Menaikkan environment class tidak memperbaiki error kode. CloudTrail hanya membuktikan file ter-upload, bukan kenapa file gagal di-parse. Membuat ulang environment memakan waktu lama dan tidak menyelesaikan bug di file DAG. Aturan umum: troubleshooting MWAA dimulai dari log yang relevan di CloudWatch Logs.","r":["Benar — DAG processing logs menampilkan error parsing/import untuk file DAG yang tidak muncul.","Salah — Masalahnya hanya satu DAG; kapasitas bukan penyebabnya, dan update environment memakan waktu.","Salah — CloudTrail hanya mencatat panggilan API upload, bukan error parsing DAG.","Salah — Membuat ulang environment mahal waktu dan tidak memperbaiki kesalahan di kode DAG."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'DAG tidak muncul di UI MWAA' → cek DAG processing logs di CloudWatch (biasanya import/syntax error atau paket hilang di requirements.txt)."},{"id":"E2A-39","d":2,"ts":"2.1.5","t":"Redshift federated queries","q":"A data warehouse in Amazon Redshift contains historical sales. Analysts need to join it with the current inventory levels that are stored in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL operational database. The inventory data changes every few seconds, and the analysts need the latest values without building an ETL pipeline. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon Redshift federated queries by creating an external schema that references the Aurora PostgreSQL database.","Unload the inventory table from Aurora to Amazon S3 every hour and query it with Redshift Spectrum.","Use AWS DMS to copy the inventory table into Redshift once per day.","Create a Redshift materialized view on the local sales table and refresh it every hour."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'latest values', perubahan 'every few seconds', dan 'without building an ETL pipeline'. Redshift federated query memungkinkan Redshift melakukan query langsung ke Amazon RDS/Aurora PostgreSQL dan MySQL melalui external schema, sehingga data operasional terkini bisa di-join dengan tabel warehouse tanpa memindahkan data. Distraktor terdekat adalah unload per jam ke S3 dengan Spectrum: dapat di-query, tetapi datanya bisa terlambat hingga satu jam dan memerlukan proses ekspor. DMS harian terlalu lambat dan merupakan pipeline tambahan. Materialized view pada tabel lokal tidak membawa data inventory dari Aurora. Aturan umum: query data live di RDS/Aurora dari Redshift tanpa ETL → federated query; data di S3 → Spectrum.","r":["Benar — Federated query membaca data terkini dari Aurora PostgreSQL secara langsung dan dapat di-join dengan tabel Redshift tanpa ETL.","Salah — Unload per jam membuat data terlambat dan memerlukan pipeline ekspor yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — Salinan harian tidak memberikan nilai terkini dan DMS menambah pipeline yang harus dikelola.","Salah — Materialized view pada tabel lokal tidak mengakses data inventory di Aurora."],"k":"Live operational data in RDS/Aurora (PostgreSQL/MySQL) queried from Redshift without ETL → federated query."},{"id":"E2B-51","d":2,"ts":"2.3.5","t":"S3 Object Lock legal hold","q":"A company's S3 Lifecycle rules delete invoice files after 5 years. The legal department has just been notified of a lawsuit and requires that 2,000 specific invoice objects be preserved until the case is closed, which may take an unknown amount of time. Other invoices must continue to follow the normal Lifecycle deletion. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Disable the Lifecycle rule for the whole bucket until the case is closed.","Enable S3 Object Lock on the bucket and place a legal hold on the 2,000 objects, removing it when the case is closed.","Apply an Object Lock retention period of 10 years in compliance mode to the 2,000 objects.","Copy the 2,000 objects to S3 Glacier Deep Archive in another bucket."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'specific invoice objects', 'until the case is closed' dan 'unknown amount of time'. Legal hold di S3 Object Lock melindungi versi objek dari penghapusan tanpa tanggal kedaluwarsa, sampai legal hold dilepas oleh pengguna dengan izin s3:PutObjectLegalHold. Lifecycle tidak dapat menghapus versi yang sedang dalam legal hold, sementara objek lain tetap mengikuti aturan normal. Mematikan Lifecycle untuk seluruh bucket melanggar kebijakan penghapusan untuk invoice lain. Retensi compliance 10 tahun memaksa penyimpanan terlalu lama dan tidak bisa dipersingkat setelah kasus selesai. Menyalin ke bucket lain tanpa proteksi WORM tidak mencegah penghapusan. Ingat: durasi tidak diketahui → legal hold; durasi tetap → retention period.","r":["Salah — Mematikan lifecycle untuk seluruh bucket membuat data lain tersimpan melebihi kebijakan.","Benar — Legal hold melindungi objek tertentu tanpa batas waktu sampai dilepas, dan objek lain tetap mengikuti lifecycle.","Salah — Retensi compliance tidak bisa dipersingkat, sehingga data tersimpan lebih lama dari yang dibutuhkan.","Salah — Salinan di bucket lain tidak dilindungi dari penghapusan dan menambah duplikasi data."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'preserve until case closed / indefinite' → S3 Object Lock legal hold."}]});